"hadiths[649]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, a person said: O Messenger of Allah! If a man commits a sin in Jahiliyyah (before the introduction of Islam), will he be impeached? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \The person who did good deeds after embracing Islam will not be impeached for the sins of Jahiliyya (even) in his era"
2,"Wazin bin Ata al-Khuza'i narrated that a person came to the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of Allah! We were in ignorance and used to worship idols, we used to kill children. I had a daughter, when she started to understand and was happy with my call, one day I called her, she started following me, I came to a well of my dear one which was nearby, I took her hand and pushed her into the well, she kept calling Abba Jaan, Abba Jaan, these were her last words. The eyes of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became tearful, and tears began to flow. One of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have made the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sad. So he said: \Surely Allah has forgiven the sins of ignorance"
3,"It was narrated on the authority of Mujahid that my freed slave Saib bin Abi Saib narrated that his family gave him a bowl of milk and butter and sent him to his idols. Sayb said: Fear of idols prevented me from eating butter, but a dog came and licked the milk and butter, then it urinated on the idols of Asaf and Naila. Narrated Harun said: In the days of Jahiliyyah, a man used to take four stones with him (from Makkah), three stones for making a hearth and the fourth stone for worship."
4,"It is narrated from Abu Raja that in the days of ignorance, if we found a good stone, we would start worshiping it, and if we could not find a good stone, we would collect some sand, then we would bring a well-milked camel, spread its legs and express its milk on this pile of sand and water it well, then we would continue to worship this pile as long as we stayed in that place. \n Imam Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: \Safi\"" refers to a camel that gives a lot of milk"
5,"It was narrated from Abu Salih Zakwan that Sayyiduna Ka'b said: We have seen it written: Muhammad, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, is the Messenger of God, neither foul-mouthed, nor hard-hearted, nor noisy in the markets, nor does he reward evil for evil, instead, he acts with forgiveness and mercy. Who will sing songs of Allah's greatness while climbing every hill and will recite Sanakhwani while stopping at every floor. They will wear Azar up to half their legs and perform ablution of their hands and feet. Their preacher calls out to the heavens that their alignment in prayer and on the battlefield is the same. Their humming in the night is like the buzzing of bees, the place of birth of the Prophet (PBUH) will be Makkah and the place of migration (Madinah) will be Tayyaba and the kingdom will be as far as Syria."
6,"Abdullah Ibn Salam used to say: We find (in the Torah) the description of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as follows: We have sent you as a witness, as a bearer of glad tidings and as a warner and as a guardian of the uneducated people. does, and I will never seize his soul until he straightens a crooked nation with the testimony of \La ilaha illa Allah\"" and the blind eyes are made blind by it and the deaf ears are opened and the veils of veiled hearts are opened. \n Atta bin Yasar said: I was informed by Abu Waqid al-Laithi that he heard Hazrat Ka'b al-Ahbar also say the same as narrated by Abdullah bin Salam."""""
7,"It is narrated from Ka'b al-Ahbar in the first line: Muhammad is my favorite servant (who is not bad-tempered, nor hard-hearted, nor noisy in the markets, nor repays evil for evil, but rather forgives and forgives, his place of birth is Makkah, and his place of migration is Madinah Tayyaba, and his rule is as far as Syria). \n In the second paragraph, it says: Muhammad is the messenger of Allah, his ummah is very praiseworthy, who will praise Allah in good times and in trouble, praise Allah on every floor and sing the praises of Allah on every mound (high ground), watch the sun, pray when it is time to pray, even if they are on a pile of garbage, wear half-shin Azar, perform ablution of hands and feet. Their sounds in the night will be like the buzzing of a bee in the sky."
8,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) inquired from Ka'b Al-Ahbar that what attributes of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) do you find in the Torah? So Ka'b said: We see this in the Torah: Muhammad bin Abdullah will be born in Makkah, will migrate to Taba (Madinah), his rule will last until Syria, he will not be obscene or noisy in the markets, he will not repay evil for evil, but he will forgive and forgive. Your ummah will be very pious, who will praise and glorify Allah Almighty (in every situation) in trouble and happiness, say Allahu Akbar on every hill and height, perform ablution on their hands and feet and tie azaar on their waists, line up in prayer as they line up on the battlefield, their humming in the mosques will be like the buzzing of bees, whose call will be heard in the heavens."
9,"Jubayr bin Nafir Hadrami narrated that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \There have come to you messengers who are neither weak nor lazy"
10,"It was narrated from Aamir that one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in need of him, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, walked with him (into the house). He was just one step inside and one step outside when he realized that he was whispering to someone. Allah Almighty said: \We have given you the Qur'an which is a judge of (right and wrong) and we have given you peace and tranquility for patience"
11,"Atiya listened to Rabi'a Jarshi, who used to say that (an angel) came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Your eyes should sleep, your ears should listen and your heart should understand. entered and ate from the table, and the owner of the house was also pleased, and whoever did not accept the invitation of the inviter could not enter the house, nor could he eat anything from the table, and the owner of the house was also angry with him. In this hadith, Malik refers to the Most High and Da'i Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he is the Dar (house) of Islam and the Table of Paradise."
12,"It was narrated from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, went out to the gravelly ground. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, was with him. He made him sit down and drew a circle around him and said: \Stay inside that circle because many people will come to you. You should not talk to them"
13,"Sayyidna Utbah bin Abdul Salmi (RA), who was among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH), narrates that a person asked the Messenger of Allah (PBUH): O Messenger of Allah! What was your initial condition? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \My foster mother belonged to the tribe of Bani Sa'd bin Bakr. I went out with her son with her sheep. We had nothing to eat or drink with us. I said (to my foster brother): O brother"
14,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghafari, may Allah be pleased with him, I said: O Messenger of Allah! How did you know and then believe that you are a prophet? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \O Abu Dharr! Two angels came to me while I was on the stony ground of Makkah. One of them was coming to the ground"
15,"It was narrated from Abu Salih that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to call them and say: \O people! I am a gift of mercy.\"""""""
16,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) that we were on a journey with the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) when a Bedouin came and when he approached him, the Prophet (PBUH) said: \Where do you intend to go?\"" He said: \""I intend to go to my family.\"" He said: \""Do you want improvement?\"" Asked: What is that? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: (That is) bear witness that there is no god but Allah"
17,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) that I went on a journey with the Prophet (PBUH). You used to disappear so far away that you would not even be seen. We camped in a flat field where there were no trees or mountains. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Jabir! Fill your bucket with water and come with us.\"" Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) said: We walked and disappeared from the eyes of the people and reached two trees with a distance of four cubits between them. Join a tree so that I may sit under your cover.\"" He went and said so. So that tree joined another one and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat behind it (for ablution)"
18,It was narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may God be pleased with him) that we went with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to the garden of Banunjar. Then he turned (to the people) and said: \There is no one on the earth and in the sky who does not know that I am the Messenger of Allah
19,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas that a woman brought her son to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, and said: My son has a disease of insanity, because of which he takes our midday and evening meals and spoils them. went, in one tradition, and the boy was healed."
20,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Jabir bin Samrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \I recognize the stone that used to greet me in Makkah before the Prophethood. I still recognize this stone.\"""""""
21,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (RA) that we went out with the Prophet (PBUH) to some suburbs of Makkah, and whatever mountain and tree came before him, he said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah."
22,"It was narrated from Shammar bin Atiya that a person from Muzaina or Jahaina said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered the Fajr prayer, and suddenly about a hundred wolves appeared and sat in their designated seats. Inform the compulsion”, the people did so, so they all went back shouting."
23,It was narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) that Gabriel (A.S.) came to the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W.). Do you want me to show you a sign (of God's power)? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Yes
24,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, that a person from Banu Umar came to the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: \Shall I show you a sign?\"" He said"
25,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) called Sayyiduna Bilal (RA), he searched for water, then came and told him that no water was found. They came to him with a musket, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his blessed hand on it, and a spring gushed out from under the paw of his hand, and Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) started drinking from it."
26,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) that when we went out with the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) for a campaign, our number was more than 210. When the time for prayer came, the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Do the people have any water?\"" A man came running with a bucket with a little water in it. The people had no water at all except that. The Messenger of Allah"
27,"Salim bin Abi al-Jaad said: I heard Sayyiduna Jabir (may God be pleased with him) say: We were thirsty (this is the incident of the Peace of Hudaybiyah), we wept and came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. drank water and it was sufficient for all of us (in the tradition of Bukhari: drank and performed ablution), in the tradition of Amr bin Marah that we asked Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) how many people were there at that time? Said: (1500) were fifteen hundred (1400 is fourteen hundred in Bukhari), even if we were one hundred thousand, that water would have been enough for us."
28,It was narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complained to him of thirst.
29,"When Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud heard about the sinking of the earth, he said: We used to regard miracles as a blessing, but you consider them a source of fear. Once we were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and the water ran out. (Like a fountain) began to flow, then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Come to the blessed water"
30,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may God be pleased with him) that there was an earthquake during his time. When he was informed about it, he said, \We"
31,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver the sermon with the support of a tree trunk, then when it became a pulpit (and he visited it) (as narrated by al-Bukhari), the trunk began to cry until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to it and placed his hand on it."
32,"Abdullah bin Burida narrated from his father: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would give a sermon, he would stand up and he would stand for a long time and it began to wear on him. He said, \If I had known that Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would praise me for something that would give him comfort"
33,"There is a hadith on the authority of Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) that before the pulpit was built, the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) used to stand with the support of a trunk."
34,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) used to deliver sermons with the support of a piece of wood, so when the pulpit was built and the Prophet (PBUH) sat on it, the wood began to cry like a camel."
35,It was narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) that the wood wept like a she-camel whose child has been taken away.
36,"Tufail narrated from his father, Sayyiduna Abi bin Ka’b (may God be pleased with him), that when the roof of the mosque (of the Prophet) was on trunks, the Messenger of God (peace and blessings of God be upon him) used to pray near the trunk of a palm tree and deliver the khutbah with its support. ordered that the minbar was placed, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and started going towards this minbar and passed by this trunk, he began to cry like a buffalo. It remained with them until it decayed and was eaten by termites and crumbled to pieces."
37,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Saeed (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering a sermon on a tree trunk when a Roman man came to him and asked him to build a pulpit for you to stand on and deliver the pulpit, so the pulpit you see today was built for him. The narrator said that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood on the pulpit to deliver the sermon, the trunk began to cry like a baby camel crying softly."
38,"Sa'iq narrated that I heard Hasan Basri, may God have mercy on him, say that when the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah, he used to deliver the sermon by placing his back (blessed) on a piece of wood. What kind of thing do you make? He said: \Make a tree like that of Moses\"". When it became Arish"
39,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that before the pulpit was built, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver the sermon with the support of a trunk, then when the pulpit was built and he turned towards it, that trunk began to cry."
40,A similar hadith has been narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him).
41,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Sahl bin Saad (RA) that the \tana\"" near which the Prophet (PBUH) used to stand cried"
42,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would stand for the sermon on Fridays, he would rest his back on a trunk placed in the mosque. In the grief of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, he started braying like an ox and the mosque began to resound. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, went to him and hugged him, so he became silent. Then he, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \By the One in Whose hand is my life"
43,"Abdul Wahid bin Ayman Makki narrated from his father that I said to Sayyidna Jabir (may God bless him and grant him peace): Narrate such a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) that you heard from him so that I may narrate it. It was done, I went to the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of Allah! This rock has become a barrier in the trench. We sprinkled water on it and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up with a stone tied to his stomach. Give me leave, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me permission, so I came to my wife and I said: Your mother has lost you. The wife replied, I have one saa (about two and a half kilos) of barley grains and one of this lamb. Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Then we slaughtered the goat and the lamb and I took off its skin and put it on the handi and kneaded the dough. And said that we have a little food, if you think fit, you should go yourself and take two men with you. He asked: \How much food is there?\"" Said there is a goat and a lamb. He said: \""Go to your wife and tell her not to take the pot off the stove and not even take the bread out of the oven until I come.\"" Then he said to all the people: \""Let's go to Jabir's house.\"" Saidna Jabir (RA) says: I was so ashamed that only God knows. He asked you how much to eat? I said yes"
44,"Narrated Anas bin Malik: Sayyidna Abu Talha said to (his wife) Sayyida Umm Salim, may Allah bless him and grant him peace: Prepare food for the Messenger of Allah. Sayyidna Anas said: Then Abu Talha sent me to the Messenger of Allah. All those present left, Sayyidna Abu Talha said, O Messenger of Allah! I just prepared food for you? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Don't worry"
45,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Ubaid (RA) that he cooked handi for the Prophet (PBUH), and he said to him: \Give me a glove (meat of the forearm)\"" and he (PBUH) liked gloves"
46,"(Marfu' Hadith) Abu al-Nu'man informed us, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from al-Aswad, from Nubayh al-'Anazi, from Jabir ibn 'Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went out to fight the polytheists. My father, 'Abdullah, said: ""O Jabir, it does not matter if you remain among the stay-behinds of Medina until you learn to what end our affair will come. By Allah, were it not that I would leave daughters behind me, I would have loved to be killed before your eyes."" He said: So while I was among the stay-behinds, my aunt came with my father and my uncle to bury them in our graves. A man caught up with them, calling out: ""The Prophet (ﷺ) commands you to return the slain and bury them in their places of death where they fell."" So we returned them and buried them in their places of death where they were killed. Then, during the caliphate of Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan (ra), a man came to me and said: ""O Jabir ibn 'Abdullah, the workers of Mu'awiyah have exhumed your father, so he has become exposed. A group of them went out, so I went to him and found him in the same state as when I buried him; he had not changed except for what the slain cannot avoid."" He said: ""So I reburied him. My father had left a debt of dates, and some of his creditors pressed me harshly for repayment. I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, my father was killed on such-and-such a day, and he left a debt of dates, and some of his creditors are pressing me harshly in their demand. I would like you to intercede with them so that they might grant me a respite until the coming harvest season.' He said: 'Yes, I will come to you, if Allah wills, near midday.' He said: So he came with his disciples. They sat in the shade, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent for permission, then entered upon us. I had said to my wife: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) has come to me today at midday; let him not see you, and do not harm the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in my house with anything, nor speak to him.' She spread a mat and a cushion, and he placed his head and slept. I said to a servant of mine: 'Slaughter this ewe,' and it was a fat, domesticated one. 'Hurry and finish it before the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) wakes up, and I am with you.' We did not cease working on it until we had finished."
47,It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah Abbas (RA) that Allah gave Muhammad (PBUH) superiority over all the Prophets (PBUH) and those in the heavens. The people asked: O son of Abbas! What kind of excellence has been given to the people of heaven. He replied: Allah the Exalted said to the dwellers in heaven: \Whoever among them says
48,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that some companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, were sitting and waiting for him. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came close to them and listened to his words. One of them said: It is a wonder that Allah made Ibrahim, peace be upon him, a friend from among His creatures, and Abraham, peace be upon him, is the friend of Allah. Someone said: And Adam (peace be upon him) was liked by Allah, and he chose him, then he (peace be upon him) came in front of them, greeted them and said: I heard your words and I heard your wonder that Abraham was Khalil and he is like that, and that Moses was private (whisperer) from Allah and he is like that, and you wonder that Jesus is the word of Allah and he is like that. They are, and they are also like Adam's favorite (that is, it is all right) and listen! I am (also) beloved of Allah and I am not proud of it, and I am the one who will raise the flag of praise on the Day of Resurrection under which Adam (peace be upon him) and those after him will be. There is no pride in this, and I am the first to intercede and the first person whose intercession will be accepted, there is no pride in this, and I will be the first to knock the chains of the gates of Paradise and they will be opened for me and Allah will admit me to Paradise and I will have poor believers with me."
49,"On the authority of Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “I will be the first to come out (i.e. from the grave) and I will be their guide when they are present (in the presence of Allah), and I will be their speaker when they are silent, and I will be their intercessor and intercessor when they are restrained, and I will be the one who brings good news when they are disappointed. Amongst the children of peace, I am the most honored and honorable in the sight of my Lord, thousands of servants will surround me as if they were hidden diamonds and scattered pearls."
50,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Jabir, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \I am the leader of all the messengers and there is no pride in that. I am the Seal of the Prophets. There is no pride in that. I am the first intercessor and the first person whose intercession will be accepted and there is no pride.\"""""""
51,"It is narrated from Anas bin Malik (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \I am the first person to knock on the door of Paradise.\"" Sufyan"
52,"On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \I am the first intercessor in Paradise.\"""""""
53,"On the authority of Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “I am the first person whose head will be divided on the Day of Judgment, and I will not be proud. If I ring the bell, who is this? I will answer that I am Muhammad, and I will find the mighty (wrathful one) in front of me. I will say: O Muhammad, raise your head and speak, your request will be granted, and I will raise my head and say: O my people My Lord! It will be said: Go to your Ummah whosoever has a grain of faith in his heart, I will admit him to Paradise. I will prostrate before Me (my Lord). Say: O Lord! My Ummah, my Ummah, it will be said, Go to your Ummah, and admit him to Paradise, whoever has faith equal to a grain of rye, I will come to him, and whoever I find in the heart of a grain of Rye, I will admit him to Paradise. They did not associate anyone with him. The Mighty One will say: By my honor I will free them from hell, they will also be taken out of hell and their faces will be scorched, they will all be thrown into the river of life and they will grow out of it like (greens) grow out of water, and it will be written between their eyes that they are the freed people of God. Then they will be taken and admitted to Paradise, the people of Paradise will say to them that they are the people of Hell, Jabar will say (no) they are freed by Jabar.”"
54,"Abd al-Rahman bin Ghanum narrated that Gabriel came down to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, kissed his stomach and then said: There is a hard and strong heart with two listening ears and two seeing eyes, Muhammad is the last Messenger of Allah and the Gatherer. Your morals are pure and your language is true and your soul is content. Imam al-Darmi said: \Waki'\"" means severe."""""
55,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Amr bin Qays, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Allah saw in the hour of mercy and shortened (the time) for me"
56,"On the authority of Sayyidina Muslimah Al-Sukuni (RA) that we were with the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) when a person said: O Messenger of Allah! Have you been provided with food from heaven? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Yes, food was brought to me.” He said: “O Prophet of Allah! There was some of it left, he said: \Yes"
57,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Samurah bin Jundab (RA) that a vessel full of thareed was brought to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and placed in front of the people, and from morning till noon the people took turns eating from it, one group standing and the other sitting. A man said to Sayyiduna Samura bin Jundab (RA): Was anything else put in this vessel or bowl? Sayyiduna Samra said: Why are you surprised? And they pointed to the sky and said: There was food coming into it."
58,It was narrated from Sayyidna Jabir bin Samrah (RA) that I saw the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) wearing red clothes on a moonlit night.
59,It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) had a wrinkle in his incisors (two front teeth).
60,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) that I have not seen anyone more helpful, generous, brave and beautiful than the Messenger of Allah (PBUH)."
61,"It is narrated on the authority of Abu Ubaidah that I asked Sayyidah Rabi' bint Mu'awz (RA) to inform me about the attributes of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH). She said: Son! If you see them, you would think that the sun has risen."
62,"On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, was of bright and fair complexion, his sweat was like pearls, he bent forward when he walked, and I found his palms softer than silk, and I did not find the fragrance of musk and amber that was in his blessed body."
63,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Anas that I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for ten years, and he never even said \Uff\"" to me. Not saying why you did this"
64,"It was narrated from Habib bin Khadra that a man from Banu Harish narrated to me that when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned Ma'ez bin Malik, I was with my father."
65,Sayyidina Bara' said: A man asked him: Did you see the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) like a sword (i.e. was his face long and thin like a sword?).
66,"Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was recognized even at night because of his fragrance."
67,"It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that if the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a road, whoever passed by that road behind him would recognize that he had passed through that road because of his scent or the smell of his sweat."
68,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Salama that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to eat a gift but did not accept charity. A Jewish woman from Khyber brought an offering of a roasted poisoned goat. He and Sayyiduna Bishr bin Al-Bara' (may God be pleased with him) ate some of it. When Sayyiduna Bishr bin Bara died, the Prophet called the woman and asked, \Why did you do this?\"" The woman replied: If you are a (true) prophet"
69,"It was narrated from Imam al-Zuhari, may God have mercy on him, that Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, used to narrate that a Jewish woman from Khyber poisoned a roasted goat and offered it to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. He took its glove and ate some of the meat, and a few companions also ate with him. Was mixed? He replied yes, but who told you? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The glove (the flesh of the hand) that is in my hand said to me.” He said: “Indeed, I mixed poison.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forgave him and did not punish him, and some of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who had eaten that meat died, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put his back because of that poison. Abu Hind chased him with a cow horn and a knife (Abu Hind was a freed slave of the Banu Bayazah, a tribe of the Ansar)."
70,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA): When Khyber was conquered, the Prophet (PBUH) was presented with a poisoned goat. The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Gather all the Jews here to me.\"" He said yes"
71,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) that it never happened that the Prophet (PBUH) was asked for something and he (PBUH) refused to give it. Imam al-Darmi Abu Muhammad said: Ibn Ayaina narrated that if he did not have that thing, he would have promised to give it to him."
72,Sayyidna Sahl bin Sa'd (RA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) was very shy.
73,"Narrated Abdullah bin Abi Bakr from an Arab man: On the day of Hunain, I caused trouble to the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace. I had heavy shoes on my feet with which I crushed the blessed feet of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Delivered, Allah knows best how my night was cut, when the morning came, a man calls out, where is such and such a man? I thought it was being called out because of yesterday's insolence. I was afraid and appeared in front of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he (peace be upon him) said: \Yesterday you hurt me by crushing my foot with your shoe"
74,"Imam al-Zuhri (may Allah have mercy on him) said that Gabriel (peace be upon him) said: There are no ten houses on earth that I have not seen, but I have not found anyone who spends more of this wealth than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
75,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abi Awfi, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to remember (God) more and talk less, he would pray long and give a short sermon, he would not speak evil or boast, he would walk with widows and the poor and fulfill their needs and wants."
76,"Sayyiduna Abbas (RA) said, \I will definitely find out how long the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) will live.\"" So he said: O Messenger of Allah! I know that not only people have tormented you"
77,"Dawood bin Ali said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked: Shall we make a cover for you? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \No"
78,"It was narrated from Sayyidina Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us outside in his dying disease, and his head was tied with a bandage. He accepted the Hereafter"" 79"""""
79,"Narrated to us Khalifah ibn Khayyat, narrated to us Bakr ibn Sulayman, narrated to us Ibn Ishaq, narrated to me 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar ibn 'Ali ibn 'Adi, from 'Ubayd the freed slave of al-Hakam ibn Abi al-'As, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, from Abu Muwayhibah, may Allah be pleased with him, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, who said: The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “I have been commanded to seek forgiveness for the people of al-Baqi', so go with me.” So I went with him in the middle of the night. When he stood over them, he said: “Peace be upon you, O inhabitants of the graves. May you be well off for what you have come to be in, compared to what the people have come to be in. Trials have come like pieces of the dark night, the last of them following the first; the last is worse than the first.” Then he turned to me and said: “O Abu Muwayhibah, I have been given the keys of the treasures of the world and lasting therein, and then Paradise, and I have been given the choice between that and meeting my Lord.” I said: “May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, take the keys of the treasures of the world and lasting therein, and then Paradise.” He said: “No, by Allah, O Abu Muwayhibah, I have chosen meeting my Lord.” Then he sought forgiveness for the people of al-Baqi', and then left. The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, was then taken ill with the illness in which he died."
80,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) that when “Idha jaa nasr-Allah wa al-Fatah” (Surah al-Nasr: 1/110) was revealed, the Messenger of Allah, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called Sayyidah Fatimah, may God be pleased with him, and said: “I have been informed of death.” And you will be the first among the wives to meet me"" 81"""""
81,"A marfu' hadith: Al-Hakam ibn al-Mubarak informed us: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Ya'qub ibn 'Utbah, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Utbah, from 'A'ishah, who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) returned to me one day from a funeral at al-Baqi', and he found me suffering from a headache and saying, ""Oh, my head!"" He said, ""Rather, I, O 'A'ishah, say, 'Oh, my head!'"" He said, ""What harm would it do you if you died before me, so that I could wash you, shroud you, pray over you, and bury you?"" I said, ""It seems to me, by Allah, if you did that, you would return to my house and consummate marriage with one of your wives there."" She said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) smiled, then his illness which led to his death began."
82,"It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) said in his deathbed: \Pour me seven buckets of water from seven different wells so that I may go out and take a pledge from the people.\"" Muhammad bin Ishaq doubts whether the narrator said \""Sab\"" or \""Shin\"" (both have the same meaning)"
83,"It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, was informed about the prayer during his death, so he said: \Tell Abu Bakr to lead the prayer.\"" (Sayyida Aisha"
84,"Sayyiduna Ikramah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died on Monday and his (body) was kept in ashes on Monday and night until Tuesday. He was buried on Wednesday night. (Some) people said that he is not dead. The soul has been taken up in the same way as the soul of Moses was taken to the sky. By Allah, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, will not die until the hands and tongues of all these nations are cut off. Sayyiduna Umar continued talking until his mouth began to foam from his anger. Yes, people! Bury your friend, you are very kind to Allah Almighty, Allah Almighty will not give you death twice, all of you should be killed once and you (PBUH) will die twice? (This cannot happen) You are very honorable and noble in the sight of Allah. People! Bury your master, and as you say (that death did not come to you), if it is so, then there is no difficulty for Allah Ta'ala that the soil itself finds you. By Allah! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away when he had clarified the whole path, made the halal lawful and the forbidden forbidden, married, divorced, fought, and reconciled. Any (herdsman) who takes care of goats, who takes his flock to the top of the mountains and drops leaves from trees for them with his stick, takes them to a reservoir (pond) for water, none of you will be more hardy and tireless than the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace. Wake up people! Bury your master. The narrator said: Sayyida Umm Ayman, may God be pleased with her, was crying. She was asked if she was crying for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: By God, she is not crying for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Do I not know that you have gone to a place that is much better for you than the world? The narrator of Hadith Hamad says that when Ayub reached this place, his voice was choked with tears."
85,"Makhool, may God have mercy on him, narrated that the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \Whenever one of you is in trouble"
86,"Ata, may God have mercy on him, said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whenever a calamity befalls one of you"
87,"Umar Ibn Muhammad narrated from his father that whenever I heard (saw) Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) mention the Messenger of Allah (SAW), he used to cry."
88,"It was narrated from Anas bin Malik (RA) that Sayyida Fatima (RA) said: O Anas! How did your hearts decide to throw dust on the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace? They said: O father! How close you are to your Lord, father! Paradise is your abode, O Father! To Gabriel we announce your death, O father! You have accepted the invitation of your Lord. Hammad said: When Thabit narrated these words, he wept."
89,"Sayyiduna Anas, may God bless him and grant him peace, while mentioning the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said that when he was present in Madinah, no day was brighter than the day when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us. And I was present on the day of your death, I have never seen a worse and darker day than the day you died."
90,Sayyidna Abdullah bin Salam (RA) asked the Prophet (PBUH): O Messenger of Allah! We will find you on the Day of Judgment standing before your Lord with heavy red eyelids ashamed of the Lord because of the deeds that your Ummah will invent after you.
91,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrated from the Prophet (PBUH) that this Surah “When the victory of Allah came, and I saw the people entering the religion of Allah in armies” (An-Nasr: 1, 2/110) when it was revealed. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Just as the people entered it (religion) army by army"
92,"(Mawquf Hadith) Abu Bakr al-Misri informed me, from Sulayman Abu Ayyub al-Khuza'i, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi, from Ma'ruf ibn Kharrabudh al-Makki, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, who said: 'Abdullah ibn al-Ahtam entered upon 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz with the common people. 'Umar was not taken by surprise except that he (Ibn al-Ahtam) was before him, speaking. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: ""As for what follows: Verily, Allah created the creation independent of their obedience, secure from their disobedience. And the people on that day were in dwellings and opinions differing. The Arabs were in the worst of those dwellings: people of the stone (rocky terrain), people of wool (nomads), and people of dung (filth). The good things of the world and its easy life were passed by them. They did not ask Allah collectively, nor did they recite a Book for Him. Their dead are in the Fire, and their living are blind, impure, along with countless things that are undesirable and shunned. When Allah willed to spread His mercy upon them, He sent to them a Messenger from among themselves, grievous to him is what you suffer, anxious over you, to the believers kind and merciful. May Allah's blessings, peace, and mercy be upon him. Yet that did not prevent them from wounding him in his body and distorting his name. And with him is a Book from Allah, speaking, which does not stand except by His command, nor does it depart except by His permission. When he was commanded to be resolute and burdened with jihad, he unfolded his banner for Allah's command. Allah made his argument prevail, validated his word, and manifested his call. He departed the world pious and pure. Then Abu Bakr arose after him, followed his Sunnah, took his path. The Arabs apostatized, or those who did so among them. He refused to accept from them after the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) except what was acceptable. He drew swords from their scabbards and kindled fires in their flames. Then he struck the people of falsehood with the people of truth, and did not cease severing their limbs and watering the earth with their blood until he returned them to that from which they had exited, and settled them upon that from which they had fled. He had taken from Allah's wealth a young camel upon which he rode, and an Abyssinian woman who had nursed a child for him. He saw that as a choking lump in his throat at his death, so he restituted it to the Caliph after him, and departed the world pious and pure upon the methodology of his companion. Then 'Umar ibn al-Khattab arose after him. He founded the garrison cities (amsar), mixed severity with gentleness, bared his forearms, rolled up his trouser legs, and matched every matter with its counterpart, and war with its equipment. When the freedman of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah struck him, he ordered Ibn 'Abbas to ask the people: 'Do you confirm his killer?' When it was said: 'The freedman of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah,' he gasped, praising his Lord that he was not struck by one possessing a right in the spoils (fay') who could argue that he only made his blood lawful by what he made lawful of his right. He had taken from Allah's wealth eighty-some thousand. He broke its quarters (distributed it) and disliked his children being guarantors for it, so he delivered it to the Caliph after him, and departed the world pious and pure upon the methodology of his two companions. Then, O 'Umar, you are the son of the world; its kings birthed you and fed you its two breasts, and you grew therein seeking its whereabouts. When you were given authority over it, you cast it aside where Allah cast it; you abandoned it, shunned it, and deemed it filthy except what you took as provision. Praise be to Allah who removed our burden through you and relieved our distress through you. Proceed and do not look back, for nothing is too difficult for the truth, and nothing is too humble for falsehood. I say this saying of mine, and I seek Allah's forgiveness for myself and for the believing men and women."" Abu Ayyub said: So 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz used to say regarding a matter: ""Ibn al-Ahtam said to me: Proceed and do not look back."""""
93,"Abu Al-Jawzaa Aus bin Abdullah narrated: The people of Madinah suffered from a severe famine, so they came to Sayyida Aisha (RA) with a complaint. The narrator said: The people had to do so that it rained so much that the grass grew, the camels became fat and burst with fat, and the name of this year became the bursting year."
94,"Saeed bin Abdulaziz said: During the Battle of Hurrah, the call to prayer and Iqamah was not performed in the Prophet's Mosque for three days, and Saeed bin Al-Masib sat in the Prophet's Mosque."
95,"It was narrated from Nabiyyah Bin Wahb that Sayyiduna Ka’b (RA) came to Sayyida A’isha (RA) and when the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) was mentioned, Sayyidna Ka’b (RA) said: Every day, seventy thousand angels descend and cover the grave of the Prophet (PBUH) with their wings and recite salutations and salutations on the Messenger of Allah (PBUH). Angels come and recite blessings until the earth will split and you will appear from the grave removing seventy thousand angels."
96,"Sayyidna Arbaad bin Saariyya Radiyallahu Anhu said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, led us in the Fajr prayer, then he gave us a very effective advice that brought tears to our eyes and hearts trembled. (Amir) Even if you are an Abyssinian slave, those of you who will live after me will see a lot of differences, so you must hold fast to my Sunnah and the way of the rightly guided caliphs, hold fast to them with your teeth, avoid new things (innovations) in religion, because every innovation is misguidance. Abu Asim once said: «Iyayakum wamuhadthat al-amour» means avoiding new things because every innovation is misguidance."
97,Imam al-Zuhri (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Our predecessors used to say that following the Sunnah is the means of salvation and knowledge will quickly disappear.
98,Abdullah Al-Dailami said that it has reached us that the first rise of the religion will be due to the abandonment of the Sunnah.
99,"Hasan bin Atiyah said: Whoever invented innovation in their religion, Allah Ta'ala removes the Sunnah from them like that, then Allah Ta'ala will not bring back that Sunnah until the Day of Resurrection."
100,Abu Qalaba said: The man who invented innovation made the sword (killing) lawful. (i.e. he is capable of being killed).
101,"Abu Qalaba said that those who follow desires are misguided, in my opinion their abode is nothing but hell, see as experience whoever adopts a (new) word or word, his case has reached the point of murder. Indeed, there are many forms of hypocrisy, then he recited these verses: \Among them are those who promised Allah that if He gives us wealth from His bounty"
102,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud and Sayyidna Huzaifa that they were both sitting when a person came and asked them about something. He said: Will you find out and leave? Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud turned to them and said: We have informed you about what you asked about and we have come to know about it from the Book of Allah, or what we have found in the Sunnah of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we do not have the power to issue a fatwa on what you have invented."
103,"Nizal bin Sabra said: I was present in every sermon that Sayyiduna Abdullah (Ibn Mas'ud) gave in Kufa. One day I heard him say, He was asked about a man who divorced his wife eight times. He replied that what he said happened, indeed, Allah revealed His Book and explained it, now whoever acts according to it, Allah made it clear, and whoever opposed it, by Allah, we do not have the power to oppose you."
104,"Nizal bin Sabra said: I went to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, and a man and a woman came to him with the issue of sanctity (i.e., divorce). He said: Indeed, Allah has made it clear."
105,"Ash'ath said: Ibn Sirin did not say anything from his opinion, he said what he heard."
106,Amish said: I never heard Ibrahim say anything from his opinion about anything.
107,"Qatadah, may Allah have mercy on him, said: I have not said anything from my opinion for thirty years. Abu Hilal said forty years."
108,"It was narrated on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi' that Ata, may God have mercy on him, was asked about something, and he said, \I do not know.\"" They were asked not to say anything about their opinion. He said: I am ashamed of Allah the Exalted to follow my words on the face of the earth."""""
109,"Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, said: A person came and inquired about something. He said: What is your opinion? Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, said: Don't you wonder about this man? I told him that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) says this and he says tell me your opinion, although my religion (i.e. copying the opinion of others) is more preferable to me. By Allah, I like singing songs more than expressing my opinion."
110,"Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, said: Beware of speculation, by the One in Whose hand is my life, if you speculate, you will certainly make the forbidden lawful and the lawful forbidden, so follow what has been handed down to you from the records of the companions of Muhammad (peace be upon him)."
111,"Al-Qamah said: A man came to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) and said that he divorced his wife eight times last night. Said: In a word. Asked if they want to divorce your wife, he said: Yes. The narrator said, then another man came and said that he had given his wife a hundred divorces. He said: Yes (that is, he said that I have given a hundred divorces). Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud said: So people want to divorce your wife considering divorce to be a sin, they said yes, then Sayyidna Abdullah said: Whoever divorced according to the commandment of Allah (one by one), Allah has explained it, and whoever made a mistake, We have given him over to that mistake. Binned)."
112,"Qasim said: After knowing the truth of Allah upon him, if a person lives ignorantly, it is better for him than to say something about what he does not know."
113,"Ayyub said: I heard Qasim, when he was questioned, he said: By Allah, we do not know all the things that you ask us, and if we had known, we would not have hidden it from you, nor would it be permissible for us to hide it."
114,"Abdullah bin Aoun said: Qasim (bin Muhammad al-Faqih) was asked about something, he said: I neither need advice nor am I worthy of it."
115,"Yahya said: I said to Qasim: I am being asked a question and you show ignorance even though your father was the Imam of the time. He replied: In the eyes of Allah and the one who has understanding about Allah, it is even more difficult and severe (strict matter) for me to give a fatwa without knowledge or to narrate something from an unreliable narrator."
116,"Musayyib bin Rafi said that when people faced a problem about which no influence was transmitted from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, then everyone would gather for it and consensus would be established, and the right is what they had agreed on, the right is what they agreed upon."
117,Awam bin Haushab has also mentioned the same from the second chain of transmission.
118,Wahib bin Amr Jamhi narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Do not hurry before the calamity descends. If you do not hurry before it descends
119,"Yahya bin Hamzah said that Sayyiduna Abu Salama (RA) narrated to me that the Prophet (PBUH) was asked about a matter which is not in the Qur'an and Hadith, and he (PBUH) said: \The believers will ponder over it.\"""""""
120,"On the authority of Abdullah bin Aoun, Qasim bin Muhammad said: You people ask about things that we did not ask about. And you guys argue about things we don't argue about. You discover things that I do not know what they are, and if we had known them, it would not have been permissible for us to hide them from you."
121,"Sayyiduna Umar bin al-Khattab (may God be pleased with him) said: Soon there will come people who will argue with you about the similarities of the Qur'an (verses), so you should grasp their hadiths, because the Ahl al-Sunan have a very good knowledge of the Book of Allah."
122,"Urwa bin Zubayr said: Moderation was established among the Israelites and there was nothing against the Sharia among them, then when the new generation and the captives and slaves of other nations came, they introduced their opinions (in religion) and led them astray."
123,"Hammad bin Yazid narrated to his father that one day a man came to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) and asked him about something that I do not know, so Sayyidna Ibn Umar (RA) said: Do not ask about something that has not happened."
124,"Imam al-Zuhri said that it has reached us that when Sayyiduna Zayd bin Thabit (RA) was asked about something, he used to ask: Has this event taken place? If their answer was yes, then he would narrate the hadith to them or express his opinion, and if the answer was \no\"""""
125,"Aamir said that when Sayyidna Ammar bin Yasir (RA) was asked about any problem, he asked, \Has this happened?\"" The people said: No"
126,"Sayyiduna Umar said on the pulpit: I consider the person who asks a fictitious question to be a sinner, because what is about to appear has been explained by Allah."
127,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \I have not seen better people than the Companions of the Messenger of Allah"
128,"Umar bin Ishaq said: Among the people before me, the most I found were the companions of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace."
129,"Raja bin Hayyah said: I heard from Ubadah bin Nisi al-Kindi that he was asked about a woman who died with some people and there was no guardian present, so he said: I found a group who did not torture like you and did not ask questions like you."
130,"Hisham bin Muslim Qurashi said: I was with Ibn Muhairiz in the valley of Marj al-Dibaj, and finding him alone, I inquired from him about a problem, so he said: What will you do by asking problems? I said: If there were no problems, knowledge would have been lost. They said, don't say that knowledge would have been lost. As long as the Holy Qur'an continues to be recited, knowledge will not be lost. Yes, you can say that understanding will rise."
131,"It is narrated on the authority of Imam Shaabi that Sayyiduna Umar (RA) said: People! We don't know, maybe we will command you things that are not permissible for you, maybe we will make things haram for you that are actually lawful for you, the last verse of interest was revealed in the Holy Qur'an and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not even explain it to us well."
132,"Abdullah bin Idris narrated from his uncle that when I came out from Ibrahim al-Nakh'i, Hammad (may Allah have mercy on him) welcomed me and asked me to ask eight kinds of questions."
133,"Zubayd Al-Ilami said: Whenever I asked Ibrahim about a problem, I felt disapproval on his face."
134,"Umar bin Abi Zaida said: I have never heard anyone say more than Imam Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him: \I do not know about it.\"""""""
135,"Abu Asim heard Abdullah bin Aoun saying that if Sha'bi was asked about a problem, he would abstain and Ibrahim (al-Nakh'i) would issue a fatwa. Abu Asim said: Sha'bi was better than Ibrahim in this regard according to Ibn Awn (because of his caution)."
136,"Ja'far bin Ayyas said: I said to Saeed bin Jubayr, may God have mercy on him: What is the matter that you do not open your mouth on the issue of divorce? He said: There is nothing related to divorce that I have not questioned (i.e. have not acquired knowledge of) but I do not like to declare the haram as halal and the halal as haram."
137,"Ata bin al-Saib said: I heard Abdullah bin Abi Yaali say, he said: I found one hundred and twenty Ansari Companions in this (Prophetic) mosque, any of them who narrated a hadith would wish that their companion would narrate a hadith, and if any of them were asked for a fatwa, they would prefer that another companion of theirs carry out this task."
138,"Dawood bin Abi Hind said: I asked Sha'bi: What did you do when you were asked a problem? He replied: You have asked someone who has experience of this. When someone was asked about a problem, he would ask his partner to answer, and that partner would say that you should answer, even after repetition, the turn of the question would go to the first person."
139,"Ibn al-Munkdar said: The scholar intervenes (through fatwa) between Allah Ta'ala and His servants, so he should find a way out (ie: refrain from making fatwa)."
140,"Mas'ar said: Ma'an bin Abd al-Rahman took out a book for me and swore that it was written by his father's letter. When I saw it, it was written on the authority of Abdullah. I see Allah Anhu that there is no one who fears them (the disbelievers) or fears them more than them."
141,"Uthman bin Khader Azdi said: I went to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, and asked him to make a will for me. He said: Listen! Adopt the piety of Allah and stick to it. Follow, avoid initiation."
142,"Imam Ibn Sirin, may God have mercy on him, said: People used to think that a person is on the right path as long as he is a factor in hadith."
143,"Imam Muhammad bin Sireen, may God have mercy on him, said: As long as a person is aware of hadith, he is on the right path."
144,"It was narrated from Abu Qalaba that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Acquire knowledge before it is seized, and the seizure of knowledge means that the people of knowledge perish. Beware! Refraining oneself from extravagance, too much contemplation and inventing new worships, and holding fast to the old ones. (That is, to hold on to the way of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his Companions)."
145,"On the authority of Abu Qalaba, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Get knowledge before it is withdrawn, and its withdrawal is that the people of knowledge are taken away. Keep your back, hold on to knowledge and avoid inventing new forms of worship (innovation), stay away from exaggeration, avoid contemplation and depth, and follow in the footsteps of the ancestors."
146,"Sulaiman bin Yasar said: A person whose name was Sabigh came to Madinah and started asking about the verses of the Qur'an. Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, asked for palm branches and sent for him. He asked, \Who are you?\"" He replied"
147,"Sayyida Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited this verse: «﴿He Who sent down ...﴾» (Al-Imran: 7/3) and said: \When you see people who are looking for similar verses"
148,"Shaqiq said that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) was asked about something, and he said: I do not like to make something lawful for you that Allah has forbidden for you, or to make forbidden what Allah has made lawful."
149,"Hameed bin Abd al-Rahman said that it is more dear and beloved to me not to respond to something that I am unable to know than to act with difficulty in something that I do not know. (That is, the expression of one's lack of knowledge is better than unnecessary suffering)."
150,"Ghulam Nafi, freed by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said that Sabigh (Ibn Ghusl) arrived in Egypt inquiring about some verses in the army of the Iraqi Muslims, then Sayyidna Amr Bin Al-Aas (RA) sent him to Sayyidna Umar (RA). When the messenger brought the message to him, he asked: Where is that man? He said: He is in the tent. Sayyidna Umar Radi Allahu Anhu said: Go and see, if he runs away, I will give you a painful punishment. And Sayyidna Umar called for green shoots and beat him so much that he bled, then left him, when he and his wounds were healed, then beat him again, then gave him a break, then called him to taste it, then Sabigh said: If you want to kill me, kill me once, and if you want to cure me, I swear by Allah, I am well now, then Sayyidna Umar said to him. He allowed him to go to his homeland, and he wrote to Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) that no Muslim should sit near him, and this thing was very important to this morning, so Sayyidna Abu Musa (RA) wrote to Sayyidna Umar (RA) that he had repented well and truly. Sayyiduna Umar (RA) wrote in reply, \Now allow the people to come and sit to meet him.\"""""""
151,"Ismail bin Abi Khalid said: I heard Amir (al-Shaabi) saying that a man asked Sayyiduna Abi bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) for a fatwa and said: O Abul Mundhir! What do you say about this? He replied: Son! The fatwa you are asking about, has it happened? Submitted: No. He replied, \If not"
152,"Masrooq said: I was walking with Sayyidna Abi bin Ka'b (RA) when a young man said: Uncle! What do you say about this? Said nephew! Has it happened? He said: No, so they replied: If not, then forgive us, until such a thing happens."
153,"Amish (Sulaiman bin Mehran) said: When Imam Ibrahim al-Nakhee, may God have mercy on him, was asked questions, he would only answer those questions that had been asked of him before."
154,"Hisham bin Hasan said: Imam Muhammad bin Sirin, may God have mercy on him, did not give fatwa on various fiyh issues related to shame. (i.e. in various issues of marriage and divorce. Allah knows best)"
155,"Salat bin Rashid said: I asked Imam Taaws (may God have mercy on him) about a problem and he inquired: Has this problem occurred? I said: Yes, then he said: Swear it has already happened. I said: By Allah it has already happened. Then he said: Our companions have informed us from Sayyidna Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with him, that he said: Do not hasten in the calamity before it descends, it may lead you astray. Answer correctly and say the right thing when you say it."
156,"On the authority of Amr bin Maimun from his father on the authority of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I asked Sayyidna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, about a person who found the month of Ramadan twice and (did not fast), he said: Has this happened or not? Maymoon said: No, then Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) said: Let go of the first call from such a revelation (i.e. do not ask about something that did not happen), so we told a lie about a person that he had this problem, so he replied that he should feed the poor in exchange for the thirty days of the first Ramadan, and feed one poor person every day."
157,Ubaid bin Juraj said that I was sitting in Makkah one day with Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar and one day with Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas.
158,"On the authority of Abu Wa'il, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may God be pleased with him) said: Get knowledge, none of you knows when people will come to him for questions and fatwas."
159,"On the authority of Ubaydullah bin Abi Ja'far, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The one among you who is the most daring in giving fatwas is the one who dares the most to go to hell.\"""""""
160,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said that what is not in the Book of Allah and what someone said based on his own opinion, and it is not even among the hadiths of the Prophet, then he does not know how much harm he will have to suffer when he meets Allah the Exalted."
161,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (PBUH): If a fatwa is given to a person without evidence, then his sin is on the one who gave the fatwa."
162,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Whoever gives a fatwa with the intention of being made, his sin will be on him (the one who gave the fatwa)."
163,"It was narrated from Maimon bin Mehran that when a dispute came to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr, he would turn to the Holy Qur’an, and if he found a solution in it, he would decide accordingly. Know anything about this matter? Sometimes, some people would tell the decision of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) unanimously. On this, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) would say: Thanks be to the One who created among us such people who remember the sayings of their Prophet (PBUH), and if they did not find any Sunnah of the Messenger, they would gather selected elders and consult with them and issue a decision according to what they all agreed on."
164,"Abu Sahl (Nafi' bin Malik al-Asbahi) said that my wife was required to fast for three days in Masjid al-Haram. Ibn Shihab said: There is no I'tikaf without fasting. Umar bin Abdul Aziz said to him: Has anything like this been narrated from the Messenger of Allah, may God's prayers and peace be upon him? Zahri said: No, he said: Did Sayyiduna Abu Bakr say something like that? He said: No. He said: So did Sayyiduna Umar (RA) say that? Answered: No, Umar bin Abdulaziz said: I don't think it is necessary to fast on it. After that, I left there and I met Taos and Ata bin Abi Rabah, so I asked them about this issue, so Taos replied that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, did not consider fasting necessary in such a case (i.e. in the Itikaaf of Nazr) unless he had the intention of fasting as well. Ata said, I have the same opinion."
165,"It was narrated on the authority of Abu Nazrah (Munzeer bin Malik) that when Abu Salamah came to Basra, I and Sayyidna Hasan (RA) went to him. He asked Sayyidna Hasan (RA): Are you Hasan? I do not want to meet anyone else in Basra more than you, and this is because I have come to know that you give fatwas based on your own opinion (so listen)."
166,"It was narrated from Jabir bin Zayd that when Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (R.A.) met him while doing Tawaf, he said: Abul Shusha'a! You are one of the jurists of Basra, so give fatwa only from the spoken and passed Sunnah of the Qur'an. If you go against it, you will destroy yourself and destroy others."
167,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: A time has passed upon us that we did not give fatwas and we were not qualified for it, but Allah Almighty has decreed it and you see the situation we have reached. And if there is a matter that is not found in the Book of Allah, then he should decide as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decided, then if a problem comes up that is not in the Book of Allah and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not make such a decision, then he should make the same decision as the predecessors did, and not say that I am afraid or I have this opinion, because the forbidden is clear and the halal is also obvious, and some matters are similar between the forbidden and the halal. Leave that which is in doubt and embrace that which has no doubt."
168,"It was narrated from Ubaidullah bin Abi Yazid that when Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about a problem, if it was mentioned in the Holy Qur’an, he would tell it, if it was not in the Holy Qur’an, and if it was found in the hadith of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, then he would tell it, and if it was not in the hadith, he would look at the fatwa of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr and Umar (may God be pleased with him)."
169,"On the authority of Qazi Shareeh, Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) wrote to him: If a matter comes to you that is in the Holy Qur’an, then decide according to it, and do not go to the (opinions) of the people, and if a matter comes to you that is not in the Book of Allah, then look at the Sunnah of the Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, and decide accordingly, and if a matter comes to you in which there is no guidance regarding it in the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of the Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, then look at the gathering of people about it. Adopt it, and if a problem arises that is not in the Book of Allah, nor in the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, nor has anyone said anything about it before you, then adopt one of two things, if you want, express your opinion by doing ijtihad, and if you want, take pause, and I consider pause to be better for you."
170,"Sayyidna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) narrated that when the Prophet (PBUH) sent him to Yemen, he asked, \If a case comes to you"
171,"Harith bin Zaheer said: I think that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: A time has passed upon us that we did not ask any questions, as if we were not in that time, and Allah has decreed that now I have reached this state as you see, so when you are asked about something, look for it in the Book of Allah. If you can't find it, then look at what the Muslims have agreed on. If you don't find that issue even in the consensus of the Muslims, then think and think and do ijtihad, and don't say that I am afraid or afraid, surely the halal is obvious and the forbidden is also clear."
172,Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid also narrated the above effect from Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud.
173,"Qasim bin Abd al-Rahman narrated from his father, he narrated in the same way from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud."
174,"Amish (Sulaiman bin Mehran) narrated that Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) said: People! You will invent new things and new things will be invented for you, so when you see something new, you must take action. Narrator Hafs bin Ghiyath said: I used to narrate this effect on the authority of Habib (bin Thabit) on the authority of Abi Abd al-Rahman al-Salami, but then I became doubtful about it, (and he narrated this hadith on the authority of Amish on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) in which there is an interruption)."
175,"Imam Muhammad bin Sirin, may God have mercy on him, said that Sayyidna Umar (RA) said to Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Masoud (RA): I have heard that you give fatwas even though you are not rich, so leave what is worthy of it."
176,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Mas'ud Radiyallahu Anhu said: \Anyone who answers whatever is asked of him is a madman.\"""""""
177,"Sayyiduna Huzaifa (RA) said: Three types of people can give fatwa, an Imam or a ruler or a person who is a scholar of abrogation and abrogation of the Qur'an. People asked: Who can be like that? He said: Either Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, or else a troublesome fool."
178,"Sayyiduna Huzaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: One of the three can issue a fatwa. He who has the knowledge of abrogation and abrogation, people said: Who is like that? He said: Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, or an emir to whom a fatwa has been given and there is no other choice, or a fool who causes trouble. Then Muhammad bin Sirin, may God have mercy on him, said: I am not one of these two (i.e. ruler and governor), and I wish not to become the third (fool)."
179,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Whoever among you has knowledge, let him reveal it, and whoever does not know, let him say about what he does not know: \I do not know\"" (i.e. I do not know)"
180,"It is narrated from Abul Muhlab that Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) said during the sermon: He who has knowledge should teach the people, and be careful not to say anything about what he does not know."
181,"Abul Bakhtri and Zazan said: Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: How cold is the liver when I am asked about something that I do not know and I say \Allah knows best\"" \""Allah knows best\""."""""
182,"Narrated Abul Bakhtri: Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: No matter how good it is (chill in the liver), of that which you do not know, say: \Allah knows best.\"""""""
183,"It was narrated on the authority of Abu Numan Razin that Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (RA) said: When you are asked about something that you do not know, run away from its answer. Razin said: Amirul Momineen! Tell me how to run away? He said: Say \Allah knows\""."""""
184,"It was narrated from Ezra Tamimi that Sayyiduna Ali said three times: The kidney is cold. The people said: What is it, O Commander of the Faithful? He said: That a man is asked about something he does not know and he says: \Allah knows best.\"""""""
185,"Hisham bin Urwa narrated from his father (Urwa) that a man asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar about a problem and he said: I do not know about it. When the man left, Sayyiduna Ibn Umar said: What Ibn Umar said is correct."
186,Imam al-Shaabi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: «La Adri» (saying I do not know) is half of knowledge.
187,"Nafi said: A man came and asked Sayyiduna Ibn Umar about something, so he said: I do not know, then when the man left, he turned and said: What Ibn Umar said is correct. They are asked about something of which they do not know, so they say: I do not know (i.e. from themselves)."
188,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Mughirah that when Sayyiduna Amir al-Shaabi was asked about something, he used to say, \La Adri\"" (I do not know)."""""
189,It was narrated on the authority of Ash'at that Imam Muhammad bin Sireen (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \If I am asked
190,"It was narrated from Amish that I never heard Imam Ibrahim al-Nakhee, may God have mercy on him, say that this is halal and this is haram, rather he used to say that people called it makruh or people considered it mustahab."
191,"It was narrated on the authority of Shaqiq (bin Salamah) that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: What will you do when you are surrounded by temptations in which the young will become old and the child will become young, and people will make these temptations (innovations) into Sunnah, and when an attempt is made to change them, people will say: The Sunnah has been changed. People asked: Abu Abd al-Rahman! When will this happen? He said: When your readers (scholars) will be many and the jurists will be few, the nobles will be many but the trustworthy will be few."
192,"It is narrated from Al-Qamah that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: What will you do in the time of tribulation when the old man and the child grow up in these tribulation? When something (innovation) is abandoned in these temptations, it will be said that the Sunnah has been abandoned. People said, \When will this happen?\"" He said: When your scholars will disappear and there will be a lot of ignorant people"
193,Imam Uza'i (may God have mercy on him) said: I was informed that it used to be said: Death is for the one who acquires fiqh in any matter other than worship and for those who consider sacred things lawful through doubts.
194,"It is narrated from Masrooq that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The year that will come upon you will be worse than the previous year. My intention is not that one year will be more lush and green than the other, nor is it that one rich person will be better than another. It means that your scholars and jurists will leave, and you will not find their successors, and people will come who will take matters into their own hands. Will speculate on the basis of your opinion."
195,"Imam Muhammad bin Sireen, may God have mercy on him, said: The first person who made guesses was Iblis, and it was because of guesses that the sun and the moon were worshipped."
196,"It was narrated from Matar (Al-Wuraq) that Hasan, may God have mercy on him, recited this noble verse: «﴿Khalaqtani min nar"
197,Masrooq said: I am afraid to speculate and my step will slip. (i.e. to fall into error).
198,"Imam Shaabi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: By Allah, if you make Qiyas the standard, then you will make the halal haram and the haram halal."
199,"Imam Amir Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, used to say: For me, saying \what is your opinion\"" is the most hateful thing. And Aamir did not speculate."""""
200,Zubarqan said: Abu Wail forbade me to sit with the people of opinion and speculation.
201,"Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, said: If these Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were in the time of the Holy Prophet, then in the Holy Qur'an it would generally be found: «Yasalunk, Yasalunk» (that is, the verses were revealed in this form)."
202,"It was narrated from Abu Hamza Maimon that Imam Ibrahim al-Nakhi, may God have mercy on him, said to me: O Abu Hamza! I have spoken and if there was a choice, I would not have spoken, surely this time in which I have become the jurist of the people of Kufa is a bad time."
203,It is narrated on the authority of Mujahid that Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Beware! Avoid speculations (philosophies) in words and actions.
204,"Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, said: I went to (the judge) Shareeh, may God have mercy on him, and a person from Murad (tribe) came to him and asked: Abuamiyyah! What is the size of the fingers? Answered: Ten camels for each finger, he joined the thumb and little finger and said: Subhan Allah! Are these two equal? Qazi Shareeh, may Allah have mercy on him, said: Subhan Allah! Are your ears and hands equal? If the ear is covered with hair or a turban, then it has half of the deity (of a man), and in the hand (not so) it also has half of the deity. It is bad for you, the Sunnah precedes your speculations, so follow the Sunnah and do not invent innovations, and as long as you hold on to the hadith, you will not go astray. Abu Bakr al-Hazli (the narrator) said: Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, said to me: O Hazli! If a crippled man of yours is killed, or a baby in the cradle is killed, will not the death of both be equal? I said: Yes! Both of them are equal, he said: Then where did the speculation go?"
205,"Sayyidna Mu'adh bin Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Holy Qur'an will become easy for the people until women, children and men will all read it. A man will say: I read the Holy Qur'an but I am not followed. By Allah, I will definitely recite it again, perhaps I will be followed, so he will read it again and still no one will follow him. It did not help, now I will build a mosque in my house, maybe I will be followed, so he will build a mosque in his house, but if it is not followed, he will say: I recited the Qur'an but I was not followed, I stood with it but it was not followed, I built a mosque in my house but it was not followed. By Allah, now I will bring to them such things that they will find in the Book of Allah Almighty and have not heard from the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, perhaps they will follow me at that time. Sayyidna Mu'adh said: Beware! Avoiding what he tells (except the Qur'an and Sunnah) and what he brings is misguidance."
206,"On the authority of Malik bin Mughal, Imam Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, said to me: Take what these people tell you about the hadith of the Messenger of God, and throw away what they tell you based on their own opinion."
207,"On the authority of Zayd bin Habab, Raja bin Abi Salama informed me that I heard Abdah bin Abi Lababa saying: I am happy with my contemporary companions who do not ask me anything, nor do I ask them any questions. One of them says: What is your opinion, what is your opinion?"
208,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu: One day the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, drew a letter in front of us and said: \This is the path of Allah.\"" Then he recited this verse: \""And this is a straight path"
209,"(The commentator of the Qur'an) Mujahid, may God have mercy on him, said in the Tafsir of \Wala ta'ttabbiuwa al-Sabul\"" that is"
210,"Amr bin Yahya reported that I heard from my father, he narrated from his father that we used to sit at the door of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) before the Zuhr prayer, and when he left (the house), we would go with him to the mosque. came out We said: No, they have not come out yet, so they also sat with us, so when Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (RA) came out, we all stood for him. Sayyidna Abu Musa (RA) said: 'Abu Abd al-Rahman! I have just seen something in the mosque that disgusts me, although Alhamdulillah it will be better and better. He said: You will see for yourself when you reach there, then he said: I saw a group of people sitting in circles waiting for prayer, in each circle there is a man with pebbles in his hands. He says: Say Subhan Allah a hundred times, then they say Subhan Allah a hundred times like this. Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: Then what did you say to them? He said: I did not say anything to them waiting for your opinion or order. Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud said: Why didn't you order them to count their sins with these pebbles and you gave them a guarantee that none of their good deeds were wasted? Then they left, we also left with them until we came to one of these circles and stood up and said: What am I seeing you doing? He said: Abu Abdul Rahman! These are pebbles, we count the number of Takbeer Tahleel and Tasbeeh through them. Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud Radiyallahu Anhu said: Count your bad deeds, then I guarantee that none of your good deeds will be wasted, O Ummah Muhammad! How quickly you fell into destruction and destruction. Now there are many companions of your Prophet, peace be upon him, and even the clothes of the Prophet, peace be upon him, have not become dirty, nor have his vessels broken. He said: O Abu Abdul Rahman! Our intention was only goodness and goodness, Sayyiduna Ibn Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: Seekers of such goodness will never be able to achieve goodness and goodness. The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, told us that there will be a group that will recite the Qur'an and it will not descend from its throat. By Allah, many such people may be among you. Then you moved away from them. Amr bin Salamah said: We saw the common men of those circles who were shooting arrows at us with the Khawarij on the day of Nahrwan (i.e. they were supporting the Khawarij)."
211,"On the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman (Abdullah bin Habib), Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: If you follow and avoid initiation, then this is enough for you."
212,Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a sermon in front of us in praise of Allah and then said: \The best path is that of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the worst is to invent new things (innovation)
213,"It was narrated on the authority of Blaaz bin Asma that I heard Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may God be pleased with him) say, he stood up on the evening of Thursday, i.e. the night of Friday, and said: The truest word is the command of Allah, and the best way is the way of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace."
214,"Imam Ibn Sirin, may God have mercy on him, said: If a person catches innovation, he turns away from the Sunnah. (In other words, when innovations are invented, the Sunnah is left behind)."
215,"It is narrated from Sayyidna Thawban (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \I fear the imams (rulers) who lead astray in my Ummah.\"""""""
216,"Hayya bint Abi Hayya said: A man came to us at noon, I said: Servant of Allah! where are you coming from So he said: I and my companion came in search of the lost, my companion went out in search and I came here in search of shade and water. who are you So he said: I am Abu Bakr. He said: Yes, he is. Haya said: I mentioned the battle of some with others in Khasham and in Jahiliyyah, and the affection and love created by Allah and these tents. Abdullah bin Aoun inserted his fingers into his fingers, Mu'adh bin Mu'adh said the same, Ahmad and his teacher Ahmad bin Abdullah did the same. I said: O Abdullah! How long do you think this case will continue? Said: As long as the imams or authorities remain on the straight path. I said: What is meant by Imams? He said: Have you not seen that when Sayyid (Master) is in the house, people follow and obey him, so long as they remain on the right path."
217,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Dardaa, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \What I fear most about you are the leading authorities (Imams) who lead you astray.\"""""""
218,"It is narrated on the authority of Qays bin Abi Hazim that Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) met a woman from the tribe of Ahmas whose name was Zainab. He saw that she did not speak. He asked: What is the matter? It was said that she has taken a vow that she will perform Hajj in silence, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Radiyallahu Anhu said: Tell her to speak, this is not permissible, it is a ritual of the era of Jahiliyyah. The narrator said: She started talking and asked: Who are you? Answered I am a member of the refugees, the woman said: Which of the refugees are from which tribe? He said: I am from Quraysh. The woman asked: From which family of Quraysh? Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) said: You are a big questioner. I am Abu Bakr. She said, \How long will we be able to stick to the religion that Allah has given us after Jahiliyyah?\"" He said: That this condition will remain as long as your imams remain correct. He said: What is meant by imams? He said: Are there not chiefs and nobles in your nation who come and give orders and the people follow them? He said: Yes"
219,"Wasil narrated from a woman whose name was Ayeza. She said: I saw Sayyiduna Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, saying to men and women: \Whoever of you men or women of that age should follow the way of the predecessors"
220,"It was narrated from Ziyad bin Hudeer that Sayyiduna Umar (RA) said to me: Do you know what will destroy Islam? I said: No. He said: The error of the scholar, the hypocrite's debate or argument in the Book of Allah, and the order of the misleading Imams. (That is, the mistake of the scholar, the argument of the hypocrite, and the order of the misguided Imams or authorities will destroy Islam, will demolish its building)."
221,"Muhammad bin Ali said: Do not sit with the philosophers, they find faults in the verses of Allah Ta'ala."
222,"Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: By the one who has no god but your Sunnah (following) is between the transgressor and the transgressor, so you adopt this middle path, may God have mercy on you. In the past, the followers of the Sunnah were the least among the people, and in the coming age there will be the least among the people, who did not follow the rebellious people in their rebellion, and the heretics in their innovation, and remained steadfast in their Sunnah until Go and meet your Lord, so become like them by the command of Allah."
223,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Moderation of the Sunnah is better than enduring hard work in innovation.
224,"Imam Ibrahim al-Nakh'i, may God have mercy on him, said: I found the predecessors, if one of them had not transgressed as much as a fingernail, I would not have gone beyond him (i.e. would not have transgressed). It is enough to disgrace a nation that you oppose their actions."
225,"Ata bin Abi Rabah, may God have mercy on him, said in the commentary of the verse “Obey Allah and obey the Messenger and the first in command among you ....”"
226,"Ibrahim bin Adham narrated that I asked Abdullah bin Shabarmat about something that was very important to me, I said: May Allah have mercy on you, think about it."
227,Sayyidina Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said to me: \Learn knowledge and teach it to the people
228,"It was narrated by Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) sent Sayyidna Mu'adh Bin Jabal and Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) to Yemen and said: You two should have trust and obey each other, be easy and do not spread hatred. So when these two gentlemen arrived in Yemen, Sayyidna Mu'adh Bin Jabal (RA) gave a sermon and inspired the people to Islam and ordered them to understand the Qur'an and said: When you have done this, then I asked, I will tell you about the people of Paradise and Hell, so they remained silent as long as Allah's Will remained, then said to Sayyidna Mu'adh, may Allah be pleased with him: You commanded us that if we understood the Qur'an, we would ask you questions, and you would tell us about the people of Paradise and Hell, so Sayyidna Muadz, may Allah be pleased with him, said: When a person is remembered with good deeds, he is one of the people of Paradise, and if he is remembered with bad deeds, So he is from the people of hell."
229,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrated that it was said: O Messenger of Allah! Who is the most polite? He said: \He who is the most pious.\"" He said: \""We are not asking about him.\"" He said: \""Then Allah's Prophet Yusuf bin Nabiullah bin Nabiullah bin Khalilullah (is the most honorable).\"" The Companions said: We do not ask about him either."""""
230,"Sayyiduna Mu'awiyah (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: Allah, the Exalted, bestows upon him the understanding of religion with whom He wills good."
231,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \Allah"
232,Sayyiduna Mu'awiya (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: \Allah
233,"Muhammad bin Jubayr bin Mut'am narrated from his father, he heard the sermon of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Arafah during the Hajj Al-Wadaa: \O people! I do not know whether I will be able to meet you again at this place after today"
234,"Muhammad bin Jubayr bin Mut'am narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, stood near Maqam Khaif in Mina and said: \May Allah bless the person who heard my speech and memorized it"
235,"Abd al-Rahman bin Aban bin Uthman narrated from his father Aban that Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (may God be pleased with him) left Marwan bin Al-Hikam at noon. So I came to Zayd and I asked him, and he said: Yes, he (Marwan) asked me about the hadith that I had heard from the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace. It is taken to the owner, any Muslim's heart if he believes in three qualities, he will enter Paradise"" 236"""""
236,"(A marfu' hadith) Yahya ibn Musa informed us: 'Amr ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Zubayd al-Yami, from Abu al-'Ajlan, from Abu al-Darda' (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) delivered a sermon to us and said: ""May Allah brighten the face of a person who hears a hadith from us and conveys it as he heard it, for perhaps one who receives it is more understanding than the one who heard it. There are three things that the heart of a Muslim does not harbor any malice for: making one's actions sincere for Allah, giving sincere advice to every Muslim, and adhering to the community of the Muslims, for their supplication encompasses those behind them."
237,Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Whoever deliberately tells a lie about me
238,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever deliberately tells a lie about me"
239,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Zubair bin Al-Awam, may Allah be pleased with him, he heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \Whoever narrates a false hadith about me"
240,"Umar bin Abdullah bin Ya'li bin Marah narrated from his father, he narrated from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever tells a lie about me on purpose should make his abode in Hell.\"""""""
241,"Atab said, I heard Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) say: If I had not been afraid of making a mistake, I would have narrated things that I heard from the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) or that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) narrated, and this is because (i.e. refraining from narrating) that I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) say: “Whoever tells a lie about me on purpose should make his abode in Hell.”"
242,"On the authority of Ataab, a freed slave of Ibn Hormuz, he heard Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, say: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever deliberately tells a lie about me should make his abode in Hell.\"""""""
243,"Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say on the pulpit: \People"
244,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Whoever deliberately tells a lie about me
245,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Allah will not raise knowledge in such a way as to take it away from the people"
246,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Get knowledge before it ends.\"" The Companions said: O Messenger of Allah! How will knowledge cease even though we have the Book of Allah? The narrator said: The Messenger of Allah"
247,"Hilal bin Khabab narrated that I said to Saeed bin Jubayr, may God have mercy on him: O Abu Abdullah! What is the sign of people dying? Said: When their scholars perish."
248,"Sayyiduna Salman, may God be pleased with him, said: As long as the first people continue to teach others and the others continue to learn from them, good will remain."
249,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) said: Do you know what is meant by \Zahaab-ul-Ilam\"" (i.e. rising of knowledge)? We said no"
250,"Sayyiduna Huzaifa said: Do you know how knowledge will decrease? The narrator said: As the cloth shrinks and the dirham is lost. He said: No, this is also the same, but the seizure of knowledge is the seizure of scholars."
251,"Sayyidna Abu Darda said: What is the matter? Get knowledge before it is taken away, the rise of knowledge is the rise of scholars."
252,"Sayyiduna Abu Darda said: There are two types of people: the learned and the learned, and there is no good in those other than them."
253,"Sayyiduna Abu Darda said: The one who teaches goodness and the one who learns (goodness) are equal in reward, and there is no good in anyone but them."
254,Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: Be a scholar or a learner or be a listener and do not become the fourth person or you will perish.
255,"Sayyiduna Salman Farsi (may Allah be pleased with him) said: As long as the (old) people continue to teach others, good will remain, and when the (old) people die before the others acquire knowledge, the people will perish."
256,Ahnaf bin Qays said: Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Get an understanding of religion before you become a leader.
257,"Sayyiduna Tamim Dari (RA) said: During the time of Sayyidna Umar (RA), people began to take pride in building buildings, so Sayyidna Umar (RA) said: O people of Arabia! Beware of the earth, beware of the earth, Islam cannot exist without a party, and a party cannot exist without a government, and a government and an empire cannot exist without obedience."
258,"Muhajir bin Habib said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said that Allah, the Exalted, said: \I do not accept the words of every wise man"
259,Abu Zahriyyah (Hadir bin Kareeb) narrated on the authority of Allah: Allah Almighty said: \I will spread knowledge in the last days until men
260,"Imam Hasan al-Basri (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Whoever asks Allah for something from this knowledge with the intention of reward, Allah wills, he will get it (the knowledge of religion), and whoever intends to gain the world through this knowledge, then by Allah, he will get the world. That is, «﴿ And what did he have in the Hereafter﴾ from the Creator﴾» [Baqarah: 200/2] They will not have any share in the Hereafter."
261,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Do not acquire knowledge for the sake of three things (so as) to repeat with the foolish, to quarrel with the scholars by it, or to turn the faces of the people towards you by it (i.e. to make them your followers)."
262,"Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman narrated that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \If someone learns this knowledge (i.e. the knowledge of religion) in order to gain the world"
263,"A man said to Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him: O scholar (of religion), give me a fatwa, so he said: A scholar is one who fears Allah Almighty."
264,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Get knowledge, you will be recognized by it, act on it and you will be called people of knowledge. Later, there will be a time when nine out of ten people will not know the known (goodness), and only the ascetic will be able to be saved from it. Abu Muhammad said that \Nauma\"" refers to one who is oblivious to evil and \""Al-Muza'iyyah\"" refers to one who talks too much."""""
265,"Sayyidna Mu'adh Bin Jabal Radiyallahu Anhu said: After acquiring knowledge, act as much as you can, until you act, Allah will never reward you for knowledge."
266,"It is narrated from Saad that when he came to Wahib bin Munba, he asked about Hasan Basri, may God have mercy on him, that what is the state of his intellect and understanding? Sa'd told his situation, then he said that we have read in the books (Samaviyyah) that whoever Allah Almighty has given knowledge to, and he has followed the path of guidance, Allah Almighty will not deprive him of his intellect, until Allah Almighty takes hold of his soul and calls him to Himself."
267,"Sayyiduna Abu Darda' (may Allah be pleased with him) says: On the Day of Resurrection, the worst person in terms of position and rank in the eyes of Allah Ta'ala will be the scholar who does not benefit from his knowledge. That is, do not act according to knowledge."
268,"Sayyiduna Abu Dardaa (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Whoever increases in knowledge, pain also increases (ie fear of God and love for Allah increases)."
269,"Sayyiduna Abu Darda said: I am not afraid of being asked what knowledge have you acquired? Rather, the fear is that I will be told how to act?"
270,Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Abbas Radiyallahu Anhu said: Discussing knowledge in some part of the night is better than worshiping the whole night.
271,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: I divide the night into three parts: one-third I sleep, one-third I stay up and one-third I remember the hadiths of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
272,"Imam Ibrahim al-Nuka'i, may God have mercy on him, said: Whoever seeks knowledge for the pleasure of God, God gives him what is sufficient for him."
273,"Asim narrated: I asked Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, about a hadith, and he told me that hadith. He said: No, we love (attributing hadith to) those who are after the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, because if there is a deficiency or excess (in the hadith), then it should be (attributed to) someone other than the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him."
274,"Imam Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade Muhakla and Muzabnah. He said: I remember, but I prefer to say Qal Abdullah, Qal Al-Qamah."
275,"Ismail bin Ubaidullah said: When Sayyiduna Abu Dardah (RA) used to narrate a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (SAW), he would say: \Qal Kada"
276,"(Mawquf Hadith) Asad ibn Musa informed us, Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Rabi'ah ibn Yazid, who said: Abu al-Darda' (ra), whenever he narrated a hadith, would say: ""O Allah, except thus, or something like it."""""
277,"Amr bin Maimon said that I used to come to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masood RA every Thursday evening. And I have never heard him say the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. One evening he said the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his eyes filled up, the veins of his neck swelled, and I saw that the buttons were open and he said:"
278,"Imam Shaabi and Imam Ibn Seereen (may Allah have mercy on them) narrated that when Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) would narrate a hadith about the days from the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him), his face would turn red and he would say: \Like this or like that"
279,"Touba Anbri said that Imam Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, said to me: What is your opinion about such and such a person who keeps saying: Rasulullah said, Rasulullah said? I (the companion of the Prophet) sat with Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) for two and a half years and I never heard him narrate any hadith from the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) except for this hadith."
280,"Imam Shaabi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: I sat with Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) for a year, but I did not hear him quoting any hadith from the Messenger of Allah (PBUH)."
281,Thabit bin Qutbah Ansari said that Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) used to narrate two or three hadiths in a month.
282,"Abdul Malik bin Ubaid said: When Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) passed by us, we said: Narrate some of what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (PBUH)."
283,"Imam Muhammad (Ibn Sirin), may Allah have mercy on him, said that Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) used to narrate less than the Messenger of Allah (PBUH), and when he narrated something from the Messenger of Allah (PBUH), he would say:"
284,"Muhammad said: Sayyiduna Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, when narrating a hadith from the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, would say:"
285,"Sa'ib bin Yazid narrated: I left for Makkah with Sayyiduna Sa'd (may God be pleased with him), and I did not hear him narrating any hadith from the Messenger of God (may God's prayers and peace be upon him) until he returned to Madinah."
286,"Quraza bin Ka'b said that when the Ansar left Madinah, Sayyiduna Umar, while sending them off, said: Do you know why I came with you to see you off? We said: Because of the excellence of the Ansar, he said: You are going to a people whose tongues move like palm trees from the recitation of the Holy Qur'an, so do not narrate the Hadith of the Prophet from them, and I am your partner. Quraza said: That is why I did not narrate any hadith, although I also heard hadiths from him, just as my companions heard hadiths from him."
287,"Qurzat bin Ka'b said that Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) sent a group of Ansar towards Kufa, I was also among them. Then they said while sweeping the dust from their feet: You will reach people in Kufa who will have the Qur'an murmured, they will come to you and say that the companions of Muhammad have come, they will come and ask you about the hadith, so listen! \Isbagh al-Wudhu\"" is three times"
288,"Alqamah said: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said.” Then he began to tremble and said: “Naho thaun or fuq tahun.”"
289,"Mujahid said: I was with Sayyiduna Ibn Umar on the way to Madinah. I did not hear him narrating any hadith from the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, except that he said: I was with the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was brought to him a pod of dates, and he, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Among the trees"
290,Salih al-Dhan said: I never heard Jabir bin Zayd saying: \The Messenger of God
291,"Abdullah bin Shaqiq said that Sayyidna Abu Huraira (inquiring about Sayyidna Ka'b) came to him, Sayyidna Ka'b said: What do you want from him? Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: I do not know anyone among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) who is a better memorizer of his hadith than me. Sayyidna Ka'b (RA) said: Surely you will find a student of anything except the student and the student of the world one day that he is bored. Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: Are you Ka'b? Said: Yes! Said: I have come to such a one."
292,"Taaws said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked: O Messenger of Allah! Who is the most knowledgeable among people? He said: \Those who share the knowledge of people with their own knowledge and every student is hungry for knowledge.\"""""""
293,"Mu'awiya bin Qura said: I was in the circle of the elders who were addressing Abid bin Amr, a young man sitting on one side said: (People) engage in the remembrance of Allah, \Bless Allah be upon you\"""""
294,Aoun bin Abdullah said: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) said: How good is the assembly in which wisdom is spread and mercy is planted in it.
295,"Sayyiduna Abu Darda said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, when he looked up to the sky, then said: This is such a time that knowledge is being taken away from people until they will not be able to do anything from it. Ziyad bin Labaid Ansari said: O Messenger of Allah! How can knowledge be taken away from us even though we have read the Qur'an and by Allah we will definitely read it and teach it to our women and children. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \O Ziyad! Your mother wept for you. I used to count you among the wise men of Madinah. The Torah and the Gospel are with the Jews and Christians"
296,"Makhool narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \The superiority of the scholar over the worshiper is like my superiority over the lowly ones\"""""
297,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Umar Radiyallahu Anhuma said: A man cannot be a scholar until he is jealous of those who are superior to him, and does not despise those who are inferior to him, and does not ask for the price of his knowledge."
298,"It is narrated from Mas'ar: I heard Abd al-Aqla al-Taimi say: Whoever is given knowledge that does not make him cry, it is appropriate for him not to receive knowledge that benefits him, because Allah has praised the scholars, then he recited: [Al-Israa: 107/17-109] \Indeed those who have been given knowledge before"
299,"Abu Hazim said: You cannot become a scholar unless three qualities are found in you: do not oppress those who are superior to you, do not despise those who are less knowledgeable than you, and do not buy the world with your knowledge."
300,"Sayyiduna Abu Darda said: You cannot become a scholar unless you are educated, and you cannot become a scholar unless you are a doer of this knowledge, and it is enough for you to be a sin that you are quarrelsome, it is enough for your sin that you are arrogant, and it is enough for you to be a liar that you keep inventing things other than Allah."
301,"Imran Manqri said that one day I asked Hasan, may God have mercy on him, about something that he had said, O Abu Saeed! The jurists don't say like this, they replied: It is your fault, have you ever seen a jurist, a jurist is one who is shunned from the world, has an attraction towards the hereafter, is insightful in the matter of religion, and is steadfast in worshiping his Lord."
302,Saad bin Ibrahim was asked: Who is the greatest jurist among the people of Madinah? He said: He who fears his Lord the most.
303,Mujahid said: The greatest jurist is the one who fears Allah.
304,"Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib Radiyallahu Anhu said: A jurist in the true sense is one who does not disappoint people from the mercy of Allah, and does not allow them to disobey Allah, and does not declare them exempt from the punishment of Allah, and does not dislike the Qur'an."
305,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: A jurist in the true sense is one who does not disappoint people from the mercy of Allah, and does not make them exempt from the punishment of Allah, and does not allow them to disobey Allah."
306,"Ka'b (al-Ahbar) said: In the first books I find the attribute of a people who will learn for the sake of action, and will learn jurisprudence in addition to worship, and will ask for the world in exchange for the Hereafter, who will wear sheepskin, their hearts will be bitterer than aloes, they will cheat through me and cheat me, I have sworn that I will create for them a trial that will surprise even the meek and the patient. will be"
307,"Haram bin Hayyan said: Beware of the transgressor. When this news reached Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, he wrote to him, and he was afraid of it. He asked, \What do you mean by the transgressor?\"" Haram replied: By Allah"
308,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may God be pleased with him) said: Whoever among you wishes to honor his religion should not go to the Sultan, and should not be alone with women, and should not quarrel with the slaves of desire."
309,"Yunus (bin Ubaid) said that Maimon bin Mehran wrote to me: Avoid fighting and disputing in religion, and do not quarrel with the learned or the ignorant, not with the learned because he will hide his knowledge from you, and will not care about what you have done, and do not quarrel with the ignorant because he will become angry with you and disobey you."
310,"It was narrated from Yahya bin Abi Kathir that Sulaiman bin Dawud (peace be upon him) said to his son: Stop arguing because it is of little benefit, and it incites enmity between brothers."
311,"Ismail bin Abi Hakim said: I heard Umar bin Abdul Aziz, he used to say: He who makes his religion the subject of disputes (will have more mobility)."
312,"Umar bin Abdul Aziz, may God have mercy on him, wrote to the people of Madinah that whoever worships without knowledge (or separates himself for worship) will cause more corruption than reform, and whoever compares his speech with action, his speech will become necessary, and whoever makes his religion the subject of disputes, his mobility will increase."
313,"On the authority of Ja'far bin Burqan, Umar bin Abdul Aziz (may God have mercy on him) was asked by a person about his wishes, and he replied: Take the religion of the Arab and the slave as obligatory, and forget that which is different from it. Imam al-Darmi said: \Multiple movement\"" means: moving from one opinion to another."""""
314,"Imam Uza'i, may God have mercy on him, said: Umar bin Abdul Aziz, may God have mercy on him, said: When you see people gossiping about something with other common people, understand that they are laying the foundation of misguidance."
315,"Imam Uza'i, may God have mercy on him, said: Iblis said to his friends, \How do you mislead a person?\"" He said: We make him slip in every way. Iblis said: Do you dominate them by seeking forgiveness? (i.e. preventing from asking for forgiveness)"
316,"Mujahid, may Allah have mercy on him, said: I do not know which of the two blessings is greater for me, Allah gave me the light of Islam or protected me from these desires, this is a great blessing."
317,"Haba bin Juwain said: I asked Sayyidna Ali (RA) or he said: Sayyidna Ali (RA) said: If a person fasts and stays awake all his life, then is killed near the Pillar of Yamani and Maqam Ibrahim, then Allah will raise him on the Day of Resurrection with those whom he considered to be guided."
318,"It was narrated from Abu Sadiq that Sayyiduna Salman (RA) said: If a person rests his head on the Black Stone and fasts during the day and stays awake at night, then on the Day of Resurrection, Allah will raise him according to his intention."
319,"Abu Sadiq narrated on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Najd that Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Live among the people like a bee lives among birds, that every bird considers it weak and weak, and if the birds know what kind of blessing is in its stomach, then they will not despise it. Day will be with the one he loved."
320,Imam al-Zuhri (may Allah have mercy on him) said: A good opinion is the best minister of knowledge.
321,"Masrooq, may Allah have mercy on him, said: It is enough for a man to be a scholar that he fears Allah, and it is enough for an ignorant man to boast about his knowledge."
322,"Muslim bin Sabih said: Masrooq, may God have mercy on him, said: A man should have such times and gatherings in which he remembers his sins and asks Allah for their forgiveness."
323,"Sayyiduna Wathila Bin Asqaa (RA) said: When we narrate a hadith with meaning to you, that is enough for you."
324,"It is narrated from Hisham that when Imam Ibn Sirin (may Allah have mercy on him) would narrate a hadith, he would not delay in presenting it, and when Imam Hasan Basri (may God have mercy on him) would narrate a hadith, he would delay in presenting it."
325,"Jarir bin Hazim said that if Hasan, may God have mercy on him, had narrated the hadith, the matter would have been the same but the words would have been different. (Meaning means used to narrate)."
326,"Ubayd bin Umayr narrated a hadith from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (SAW) said: \The example of a hypocrite is like goats sitting in a fold. Or he is like two goats in a herd.\"" Hearing this"
327,"Abdullah bin Aoun said: Imam Shaabi, Imam Ibrahim Nakhai and Imam Hasan Basri (may Allah have mercy on him) used to narrate the hadith, sometimes in this way and sometimes in that way."
328,"Abu Mu'mar said: I hear a hadith in a style or tone, so I adopt the same style as I have heard it."
329,"Ibrahim Ibn Maisrah said that Mujahid saw Taaws, may God have mercy on him, in a dream, that he was praying in the Kaaba wearing a veil, and that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was standing at the door of the Kaaba and saying: O servant of Allah! Remove your veil, and recite aloud (i.e. narrate the declaratory hadith), Ibrahim said: He interpreted it with knowledge, and then he recited the hadith, rejoicing."
330,Ka'b said: The world is cursed and everything in it is also cursed except the one who learns and teaches good.
331,"Khalid bin Ma'dan said: People are either learned or learned, and those who are between the two are vile people, in whom there is no good."
332,"Hisham narrated that Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: People used to say that the death of a scholar is a crack in Islam, which nothing will be able to close until the end of the world."
333,"Wahib bin Munba said: To me, a meeting in which there is a discussion about knowledge is more beloved and beloved than prayer, because maybe one of them will hear a word that will benefit him for a year or for the rest of his life."
334,"Sufyan Al-Thawri, may Allah have mercy on him, said: For whomever Allah wills good, He knows no better deed than acquiring knowledge and memorizing it."
335,Hasan bin Salih said: People will certainly need this knowledge in their religious affairs just as they need food and drink in their world.
336,"Sayyiduna Abu Darda said: Get knowledge before it is exhausted. Verily, the exhaustion of knowledge is the exhaustion of the scholars. Indeed, the scholar and the student are equal in reward."
337,"It was narrated from Al-Dahhak, may God have mercy on him, that the honorable verse: «﴿Walkin kunua rabbaniyin bima kuntum tu’almoon ban al-Kitab....﴾» [Al-Imran: 79/3] means that whoever reads the Qur’an, it is obligatory for him to become a jurist (i.e. a divine scholar)."
338,"Imam Hasan al-Basri, may God have mercy on him, in his commentary on this verse: \If it were not for them to stop the Lord and the Lord....\"" [Al-Ma'idah: 63/5] \""Why do not their worshipers and scholars stop them?\"""""""
339,"Saeed bin Jubayr, may Allah have mercy on him, said about \Kunwa Rabbaniyin\"" (All of you belong to the Lord)."""""
340,"Ubaidullah bin Saeed said: I heard Sufyan bin Uyaina saying: Knowledge means memorization, action, listening, silence and preaching."
341,"Sufyan bin Uyaynah, may God have mercy on him, said: The greatest ignorant among people is the one who abandons knowledge while having knowledge (i.e. does not act or preach), and the greatest scholar is the one who acts according to knowledge, and the best among people is the one who fears Allah the Most High."
342,"Imam Hasan Basri, may God have mercy on him, said: Two greedy people never get tired, one is greedy for knowledge who never gets tired of knowledge, and the other one who has worldly desires and does not get tired of this world. will disperse him, and will write his poverty and neediness between his two eyes, then he will be poor in the morning and poor in the evening."
343,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: Two greedy men never get tired, one is a scholar and the other is a seeker of the world and both cannot be equal. Then Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) recited this verse: \All human beings do not seek refuge when they see them.\"" Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud Radiyallahu Anhu said: Someone else said: «﴿Inma Yakhshaya Allah min ’ibadahi al-ulamaa’’... (Fatir: 28/35) “Indeed"
344,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with him: «(Allah does not fear His servants of the scholars)» [Fatir: 28/35] He who fears Allah is a scholar. Two greedy men can never be comfortable, a student and a student of the world."
345,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) said: Two eager people never get bored, the student and the student of the world."
346,"On the authority of Sayyidna Wathla bin Asqaa, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever seeks knowledge and obtains it"
347,"Abbas Al-Umi said: I have received the news that Prophet Dawood (peace be upon him) used to say in his prayer: O Allah! You are pure (from every defect), You are my Lord, the glory is above the throne, and You have created Your awe in those who are in the earth and in the sky, so the closest to You among Your creatures in position and status is the one who has the most fear and awe of You, and only he who has knowledge does not fear You, and what is the wisdom that does not follow Your command."
348,"It was narrated from Dahhak, may God have mercy on him, that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: Either become a scholar or a learner, and there is no good in anyone except these two."
349,"On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Imamah, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Soon there will be such tribulations in which a person will be a believer in the morning and become a disbeliever in the evening"
350,"Harun bin Rabab said: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say: Either be a scholar or a learner, do not be between them, because between them are ignorant people. Indeed, the angels are pleased with the actions of such a man and spread their wings for him who goes forth to seek knowledge."
351,"Imam Hasan al-Basri, may God have mercy on him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about two men from Bani Israel, one of them was a scholar who used to pray and then sit and teach people the good, the other man who fasted during the day and stayed awake at night. \n The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The superiority of a scholar who prays and then sits down and teaches people good things over a worshiper who fasts during the day and recites Tahajjud at night is like my superiority over one of your lowly men.\"""""""
352,"Imam Ibn Sireen, may God have mercy on him, said: I entered the mosque (and saw) Aswad bin Saree narrating a story, and Hameed bin Abdul Rahman was having a scholarly conversation in a corner of the mosque. I felt drowsy and a visitor came and said: Do you hesitate where to sit? If you want, I can tell you the place where Gabriel (peace be upon him) sat in the circle of Hameed bin Abd al-Rahman."
353,"Kathir bin Qays said: I was sitting with Sayyidna Abu Dardaa in the mosque of Damascus when a man came to him and said: O Abu Dardaa! I have come to you from Madinah to the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) for this hadith which I have been informed that you narrate (it) from the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him). Sayyidna Abu Darda said: You have come for trade? Said: No. He said: And nothing brought you here? He said: No, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \Whoever goes out in search of knowledge on a certain path"
354,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Everything seeks forgiveness for the one who teaches goodness, even the fish of the sea."
355,"On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever follows a path in search of knowledge"
356,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) said: No man walked a path in search of knowledge, but Allah made the path of Paradise easy for him through him, and whoever delayed his action, his action will not hasten for him."
357,Matar al-Waraq said: The honorable verse: «﴿Walqad Yasarna Al-Qur’an for the remembrance of those who are of the mudkar (Al-Qamar: 17/54) means: There is a good seeker who should be helped.
358,It is narrated on the authority of Marwan that Zamra said: This «(Mud
359,"It was narrated from Amir bin Ibrahim that when Sayyiduna Abu Dardah (RA) would see the students of knowledge, he would say, \Mrhaba talaba-ul-ul-Im\"" (Welcome to the students of knowledge) and he would say: The Messenger of Allah"
360,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by two congregations in his mosque, and he said: Both are good, but one congregation is better than the other. I have been sent. The narrator said then you also visited him."
361,Matraf bin Abdullah al-Shakhir said to his son: Son! Knowledge is better than action.
362,Sharhabil bin Sharik heard Abu Abd al-Rahman Hubli say: There is no gift better than the gift you give your brother of wisdom.
363,"Imam al-Zuhri, may God have mercy on him, said: The excellence of a scholar over a mujtahid is a hundred degrees higher, and between each two degrees there is a distance of five hundred years of fast running horses. (Implied the horse that is prepared for running (races))."
364,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: “Allah raises those who believe among you, and those who attain the highest levels of knowledge.”"
365,"Hasan al-Basri, may God have mercy on him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The man who dies seeking knowledge for the revival of Islam"
366,"Amr ibn Maimon, may God have mercy on him, said: Sayyiduna Umar took away two-thirds of knowledge."
367,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Those who gather in one of the houses of Allah, recite (recite) the Book of Allah and teach it to others, the angels take them under the shade of their wings until they engage in other matters. And whoever follows the path of acquiring knowledge, Allah will make the path to Paradise easy for him, and whoever neglects his action, his lineage (family) will be of no use."
368,"It was narrated from Dhir that I went to Safwan bin Asal Moradi (because) I wanted to ask him about wiping the socks. He said: What brought you to me? I said: Seeking knowledge. He said: Shall I not give you good news? I said: Recite it, so he narrated that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Indeed"
369,"Yahya bin Yaman said: I heard Sufyan, may God have mercy on him, say for forty years: Hadith has never been more sought after than today. People asked Sufyan, may God have mercy on him: People ask hadith without intention. He said: Asking them is intention."
370,"Mujahid, may Allah have mercy on him, said: We sought this knowledge without any great intention, then Allah Almighty gave us the (righteous) intention afterwards."
371,"Imam Hasan al-Basri, may God have mercy on him, said: People sought knowledge although they intended neither Allah nor what is with Allah through it."
372,"Abu Muslim Khulani (may Allah have mercy on him) said: There are three types of scholars. One is the person who lives in knowledge and others live with him in it, the second is the person who himself lives in the world of knowledge but no one is with him, the third is the person so that people benefit from his knowledge and (he himself is inactive) knowledge will overwhelm him."
373,"On the authority of Ata bin Abi Rabah, Musa (peace be upon him) said: O Lord! Who is the wisest among your servants? He said: He who decides for people is the same who decides for himself. He said: O Lord! Who is the richest among your servants? He said: He who is most satisfied with his fate. He said: O Lord! Who is the most fearless of your servants? He said: He who has the most knowledge about me."
374,"Sufyan, may Allah have mercy on him, said: It is said that scholars are of three types: One is the one who has knowledge of Allah, fears Allah, but is ignorant of Allah's commands. Second, the one who knows Allah, and knows Allah's commands, also fears Allah, this is the perfect scholar (religion)."
375,"It was narrated from Imam Hasan Basri, may God have mercy on him, that knowledge is of two kinds, the knowledge that resides in the heart is useful knowledge, and the other knowledge (which only) remains on the tongue, then this knowledge is proof from God against the son of Adam."
376,Hasan (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to the above text.
377,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: Learn knowledge, learn knowledge, and when you get knowledge, act."
378,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: He who seeks knowledge for four things will go to hell. Or he said a similar sentence (these things are): so that he may boast of the scholars with this knowledge, or rebuke the foolish ignorant with it, fight with it, or turn the faces (hearts) of the people towards him with it, or gain something from the nobles with this knowledge."
379,"The disciple of Hisham Dastwai said: I read in a book, I was informed that this is the word of Jesus: You work for the world and you are provided with sustenance in this world without action. And you do not act for the sake of the Hereafter, although in the Hereafter you will be provided with sustenance for your actions. Shame on you scholars, you take the wages and waste the deeds, it is near that the Lord (al-Alam) will call for your work and you are near to leave this wide world and go to the dark and narrow grave. Allah Ta'ala forbids you from sins, just as He orders you to pray and fast. How can a man be among the people of knowledge who is angry with his sustenance and despises his position, even though he knows that it is from the knowledge and power of Allah Almighty? How can a man be among the scholars whose abode is the Hereafter but he is focused on this world, and who desires more than what harms him, or is more beloved than what benefits him, how can he be among the people of knowledge who seeks knowledge in order to generalize it and does not seek knowledge for action."
380,"Habib bin Ubaid said: It is said that learn knowledge and benefit from it, and do not acquire knowledge in order to gain adornment from it. If you live long, it is near (that you will see)."
381,"Ahaws bin Hakim, narrating from his father, said: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about evil, so he (peace be upon him) said: \Do not ask me about evil"
382,"Isa said: I heard Imam Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, say: The person who will seek this knowledge will have two qualities: intelligence and worship. And if he is wise and not a worshiper, he will say: Only worshipers can attain this thing, so he will leave the demand for it (knowledge). Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, said: I am afraid that those who are seeking knowledge today will not have one of the two things, neither wisdom nor worship."
383,"Abu Asim said that Sufyan, while explaining his evidence, said: A man used to worship for forty years, then he went out in search of knowledge."
384,"Makhool, may God have mercy on him, said: He who seeks knowledge in order to argue with the ignorant and foolish through it, and to boast about it with the scholars, and to turn people's hearts towards him through it, then he will be in the fire of Hell."
385,"Makhool, may God have mercy on him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever seeks knowledge in order to be proud of the scholars through it"
386,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) said: A man's words are remembered in proportion to his sincerity.
387,"Qasim said: Syedna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) said to me: In my opinion, a person who has knowledge, then he forgets knowledge because of what he commits."
388,"Shahr bin Hushab said: We have received (reached) that Luqman al-Hakim used to say to his son: Son! Do not learn knowledge in order to be proud of the scholars through it, or to repeat it with the sages, or to show hypocrisy through it in assemblies, and do not leave knowledge unwillingly and for the sake of ignorance. O son! Take care and hold meetings, so when you see a group mentioning Allah, sit with them, because if you are knowledgeable, your knowledge will benefit you, and if you are ignorant, they will teach you. And if you see a group that is heedless of the remembrance of Allah, then do not sit with them, because if you are knowledgeable, your knowledge will not benefit you, and if you are ignorant, they will increase your misery, and it is possible that Allah will punish them and you too will have to taste it."
389,"Kathir bin Murrah said: Do not tell falsehood to the wise, they will hate you, and do not speak wisdom to the fools, they will deny you, do not hide knowledge from the people of knowledge, you will be sinful, and do not teach knowledge to the unworthy, they will think you are ignorant, your knowledge has a right over you, just as you have a right over your property."
390,"Abu Farooq narrated that Jesus Ibn Maryam (peace be upon him) used to say: Do not withhold knowledge from those who have knowledge because you will be sinners, and do not spread knowledge to those who are not able to make you ignorant, be a gentle physician who keeps medicine where it will benefit."
391,Mutaraf said: Do not feed your food to a man who does not have an appetite for it.
392,"Dawood bin Sabur heard Shahr bin Haushab say: Luqman (peace be upon him) said to his son: O son! Do not learn knowledge in order to become hypocrites through it, and do not leave knowledge out of aversion to knowledge and enticement into ignorance, and when you see a group that remembers Allah, sit with them, if you are knowledgeable, your knowledge will benefit you, and if you are ignorant, they will inform you, and it may be that Allah will look upon them with mercy and you will be blessed with some of it along with them. And if you see a group that is heedless of the remembrance of Allah, then do not sit with them, because even if you have knowledge, your knowledge will not benefit you, and if you are ignorant, they will only increase your misguidance or wretchedness."
393,"Sayyiduna Ali (RA) said: O acquirers of knowledge! Act upon it, surely the scholar is the one who acts according to his knowledge, and his knowledge and actions are consistent, soon there will be people who will have knowledge but that knowledge will not descend from their throats, their actions will be against their knowledge and their inner affairs will be against the outward, sitting in circles and boasting to each other even if a man is angry with his neighbor if he leaves him and sits next to someone else. It goes, these are people whose actions do not rise from their gatherings to Allah Ta'ala."
394,"Masrooq, may Allah have mercy on him, said: It is enough for a man's knowledge that he fears Allah, and it is enough for a man's ignorance that he brags about his knowledge."
395,"Mu'awiyah bin Qura, may God have mercy on him, said: If any nation among other nations follows the lowest scholar of that nation, then that nation will be guided."
396,"Imam Hasan al-Basri, may God have mercy on him, said: If a person acquires knowledge and practices it, it is better for him than the world and the world."
397,"Imam Hasan al-Basri, may God have mercy on him, said: (Among the predecessors) when a man sought knowledge, its effect was seen in his eyes, humility, tongue, hands, prayer and asceticism."
398,"Imam Muhammad bin Sirin, may God have mercy on him, said: Look who you are taking this hadith from, because this is your religion."
399,"Bishr bin Haqm reported that I heard Sufyan, may God have mercy on him, say: The servant who increases his desire for the world with the increase in knowledge increases his distance from Allah."
400,"Hasan said: The more advanced a person is in the knowledge of God, the closer people will be to him by the mercy of God."
401,"And Hasan said in the second hadith: The more a person advances and increases in knowledge, the more he becomes correct in his intentions, and Allah Almighty has not clothed a servant with anything better than peace and contentment."
402,"Umira said: A man said to his son: Go get knowledge. The boy went out and disappeared. Then when he returned, he narrated some hadiths from his father. The father said: Go son (still) seek knowledge. He was absent for some time, then he came back with some books and papers and read them to his father, so the father said to him: This is black on white. Now go and learn knowledge. So he disappeared from them and then returned. So he said to his father: Father! Now ask me whatever you want, his father said: If you pass by a man who praises you and another man criticizes you, what is your opinion about it? The boy replied: In such a case, I will not blame the one who criticizes, and I will not praise the one who praises. The father said: If you see a sheet, what will you do? Abu Shureih said: I don't know, what will you do if you see gold foil or silver foil? He said: I will neither lift it nor go near it. The father said: Go now you have become a scholar."
403,"Sakin bin Umayr said: I heard Wahib bin Munbah, may God have mercy on him, say: Son! Hold on to wisdom and wisdom, surely all good is in wisdom, which wisdom gives honor to the small over the great and the slave over the free. And increases the nobleness of the owner, and makes the poor sit in the place of kings."
404,"Sayyiduna Abu Darda said: If it were not for the sayings of the scholars, we would be nothing."
405,"Abu Qalaba said: Do not sit with the slaves of desires (Ahl al-Hus), and do not repeat with them, because I do not consider you safe from them, that they will plunge you into error, or confuse even what you know."
406,"Ayyub said: When Saeed bin Jubir saw me sitting next to Talaq bin Habib, he said to me: Didn't I see you sitting next to Talaq bin Habib? You (never) sit near them."
407,"It was narrated from Nafi that a man came to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) and said: So-and-so man greets you. Sayyidna Ibn Umar (RA) said: I have come to know that he has invented innovation. If he has done so, do not greet him."
408,Amish said: Imam Ibrahim Nakhai did not consider saying anything about a heretic as backbiting.
409,"Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, said: The desire of the self is named \Hawa\"" because it goes down (into Hell) with the owner of Howa."""""
410,Muhammad bin Wasee said that Muslim bin Yasar used to say: Protect yourself from Mara' (showing) because this is the hour of ignorance of the scholar and the devil is looking for such a slip.
411,"Asma bin Ubaid said that two men from among the people of lust (the theologians and philosophers) came to Imam Ibn Sirin, may God have mercy on him, and said: O Abu Bakr! We narrate the Hadith for you. He said: No (there is no need for it). He said: Then we recite to you a verse of the Holy Qur'an. The narrator said: So they both left, someone from the congregation said: O Abu Bakr! What was wrong if he recited a verse of the Holy Quran? He said: I was afraid that he would recite a verse and distort it and it would sit in my heart."
412,"It was narrated from Salam bin Abi Muti' that a man from the \Ahl al-Ahwa\"" (innovators) said to Ayyub (al-Sakhtiani"
413,"It was narrated on the authority of Kulthum bin Jabr that a man asked Saeed bin Jubayr, may God have mercy on him, about something, and he did not answer it."
414,"On the authority of Abu Ja'far Muhammad bin Ali, he said: Do not sit with the people of logic (logic and philosophy) because these are the people who speak in the verses of Allah."
415,"Imam Hasan and Imam Muhammad bin Sirin, may God have mercy on him, said: Do not sit with the people of the word, do not debate with them, and do not listen to them."
416,"Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, said: The servants of desire and lust and the self are named because they will be cast into hell."
417,"Ibrahim bin Maisrah said: I have not seen anyone among the people except Imam Tawas, may God have mercy on him, to whom the Sharif and the Kamin are equal. (Ibrahim) Ibn Maisrah used to swear by it."
418,"Imam al-Zuhri (may Allah have mercy on him) said: We used to dislike writing down knowledge, but the Sultan forced us to do so, and now we dislike preventing anyone from writing down knowledge."
419,"Abdullah bin Aoun, may God have mercy on him, narrated that people asked Imam Muhammad bin Sirin, may God have mercy on him, about a man to teach him hadith (in particular), so he said: Even if that man is an Abyssinian, he and (my son) Abdullah bin Muhammad are equal in this regard. (i.e. in value and status)."
420,"Salat bin Rashid said: Salim bin Qutiba asked Imam Tawas (may Allah have mercy on him) a question about a problem, to which he did not answer. It was said: This is Salam bin Qutiba. That is, all are equal in terms of knowledge."
421,"Habib bin Salih said: I did not fear anyone more than Khalid bin Madan. (That is, because of his knowledge, he used to be in awe)."
422,Mugheera bin Muqassim said: We used to fear Imam Ibrahim Nakhai as an emir and a governor.
423,"Ayyub (al-Sakhtiyani) said: Saeed bin Jubayr narrated a hadith one day, so I stood up and said: repeat it twice. He said: I neither express milk nor drink every hour."
424,Ata ibn al-Saib said: Abu Abd al-Rahman disliked narrating hadith while walking.
425,"Habib bin Thabit said: We were with Saeed bin Jubayr, may God have mercy on him, when he narrated a hadith, and a man asked him: Who narrated this hadith from you? Or who did you hear it from? So Saeed (may Allah have mercy on him) became angry and stopped us from talking to him, until he got up and left."
426,Abu Salama said: I wish I had taken the companionship of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) then I would have acquired an abundant portion of his knowledge.
427,Umm Abdullah bint Khalid said that I have never seen anyone who respects knowledge more than my father.
428,"Sulaiman bin Musa said: I said to Imam Taaws, may God have mercy on him: Such and such a man narrated a hadith to me like this."
429,"Sa'd bin Ibrahim said: Only reliable narrators narrate hadith from the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace."
430,"Imam Muhammad bin Sireen, may God have mercy on him, said: People did not ask about the isnad at first, then they began to question (i.e., they started asking who and what kind of narrator is), they used to take hadith from him who had the authority of Sunnah, and they did not take hadith from him who was not the authority of Sunnah. Imam Darmi said: I do not think that Jarir would have heard it from Asim."
431,"Imam Muhammad bin Sireen, may God have mercy on him, said: Do not narrate the hadith you narrated to me in the manner of these two men, because they do not care who they are taking the hadith from. Imam Darmi said: I do not believe that Jarir heard this from Asim."
432,"Ibrahim Nakhai (may Allah have mercy on him) said: When you narrate a hadith from me, then narrate it in the manner of Abu Zarayah, may God have mercy on him, because he narrated a hadith to me, then after a year I asked him about the same hadith, and he did not miss a single letter in it."
433,"Imam Muhammad bin Sirin, may God have mercy on him, said: This knowledge (hadith) is religion. A man should be careful how he takes his religion from a man."
434,"Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, said: (The righteous Salaf) when they went to someone for knowledge of hadith, they used to carefully observe his prayer, form, and posture. Then he used to take hadith from him."
435,"Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, said: When they (the righteous Salaf) came to a person from whom they wanted to learn, they would observe his prayer, behavior, appearance, and then learn from him."
436,Hasan Basri (may Allah have mercy on him) also narrated like Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him).
437,"Abul Aaliyah said: We used to go to a man to take a tradition from him, and when he was praying, we would see him. Abu Mumar said: His words are like this."
438,"Imam Muhammad bin Sirin, may God have mercy on him, said: This knowledge (Ilm-e-Isnad al-Hadith) is religion, so see how you are getting your religion from man."
439,"Sulaiman bin Musa said: I told Imam Taaws, may God have mercy on him, that such and such a man narrated a hadith in this way."
440,"Imam Taaws, may God have mercy on him, said: Basheer bin Ka'b came to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) and started narrating the hadith. Sayyidna Ibn Abbas (RA) said: Recite the first hadith to me. Bashir said to him: I do not know whether you considered all my hadiths to be authentic and denied the first hadith, or did you consider this first hadith to be authentic and not the rest? Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We used to narrate hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at a time when he was not being lied to, then when people became soft and warm (i.e. lying to the truth), then we abandoned the tradition of hadith from him. (That is, when people started attributing lies to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, we began to be careful and the person who told them was investigated)."
441,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) said: We used to remember the hadith until you mixed it up, and the hadith is remembered from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
442,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said: It is near that the demons will appear, who were bound by Sulaiman (AS), who will teach people the understanding of religion and jurisprudence."
443,"Imam Muhammad bin Sireen, may God have mercy on him, said: Be careful from whom or how you are taking this hadith, because this is your religion."
444,"Mu'tamar explained to his father that the interpretation of the hadith of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, should be avoided in the same way as the interpretation of the Holy Qur'an is avoided."
445,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) said: Do you not fear that you will be punished or that you will be drowned instead of saying: \The Messenger of God said and said so-and-so\"" meaning the Messenger of God said this and so-and-so said that."""""
446,"Imam Uza'i, may God have mercy on him, said: Umar bin Abdul Aziz, may God have mercy on him, wrote that no one's opinion is (acceptable) in the Book of Allah, and the opinion of the Imams will also be accepted regarding that which is not found in the Book of Allah or the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Sunnah that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has no room for opinion."
447,"It was narrated from Ubaydullah bin Umar that Umar bin Abdul Aziz, may God have mercy on him, gave a sermon and said: People! Indeed, Allah Almighty did not send any prophet after your Prophet, nor did He reveal any book after the Book that He revealed to you, so what He made lawful in the language of His Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, is lawful until the Day of Resurrection, and what He made forbidden by the language of His Prophet is forbidden until the Day of Resurrection. Listen! I am not a judge but a critic, and I am not an innovator, but a follower, and I am not better than you except that I have a greater burden (responsibility) than you, and listen! There is no one among Allah's creatures who should be obeyed in disobedience to Allah. Listen! Did I tell you?"
448,"Hisham bin Hajeer said: Imam Taaws, may God have mercy on him, used to offer two rak'ahs of prayer after the Asr prayer, so Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said to him: Leave it. Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: Undoubtedly, any prayer after Asr has been prohibited, so I do not know whether you will be punished or rewarded for it, because Allah Almighty says: A believing man or woman has no authority over any of his commands after the command of Allah and His Messenger, and whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger, he will be clearly misled [Al-Ahzab: 36/33]. Sufyan said: \Tuttakhuza sallam\"" (meaning) He says to pray from Asr till night."""""
449,"It was narrated from Sayyidna Jabir (RA) that Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) came to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) with a copy of the Torah and said: O Messenger of Allah! This is a copy of the Torah, he (may God bless him and grant him peace) remained silent and Omar (may God be pleased with him) began to read it, the face of the Messenger of God (may God bless him and grant him peace) began to change, and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may God be pleased with him) said: Mothers who lose (lose) you, do you not see the face of the Messenger of God (may God bless him and grant him peace)? So Umar looked at the face of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I seek refuge in Allah from the wrath of Allah and the wrath of His Messenger. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: \By the One in Whose hand is the life of Muhammad"
450,"Abu Ba'ah, a man from Aal Umar, said: Sa'eed bin Al-Musayb, may God have mercy on him, saw a man praying two rak'ahs frequently after Asr, he inquired: O Abu Muhammad! (surname of Saeed bin Al-Musayib) Will Allah punish me for praying? He said no (not for praying), but for violating the Sunnah, Allah will surely punish you."
451,"On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \A man was undressing in his two cloaks"
452,"Khurash bin Jubayr said: I saw a young man in the mosque who was throwing pebbles. A sheikh said to him: Do not throw pebbles. This young man was negligent and thought that the sheikh was not looking at him, so he started throwing pebbles, so the sheikh said to him: I am telling you a hadith that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) prohibiting throwing pebbles, yet you are doing the same? By God, I will not come to your funeral, nor will I visit you if you are sick, and I will never talk to you. I said to my companion whose name was Muhajir: Go to Khurash and ask him, so he went to him and asked about it, so he narrated this hadith to him. (i.e. confirmed it)."
453,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mughfil (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (SAW) forbade throwing pebbles and said: \This pebble cannot kill a bird or harm an enemy except that it will break a tooth or put out an eye.\"" Then Saeed bin Jubayr and the person with whom there was a relation picked up something from the ground and said: What significance can this have? Saeed bin Jubayr said: Don't you see that I am narrating to you the hadith of the Messenger of Allah"
454,"Abdullah bin Burida said: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Mughfil (RA) saw one of his Companions throwing a pebble. So he said: Do not throw pebbles because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade throwing pebbles, (in another hadith) he did not like throwing pebbles, and he (peace be upon him) said: \The enemy cannot be harmed or hunted by it"
455,"Qatadah said: Imam Muhammad bin Sireen, may God have mercy on him, narrated the hadith of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, to a man, and the man said: So-and-so said this? Imam Ibn Sireen, may Allah have mercy on him, said: I am narrating to you the hadith of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and you say that so-and-so said this? I will never talk to you."
456,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \If the wife of one of you asks for permission to go to the mosque"
457,"Abu al-Mukharaq said that Sayyidna Ubadah bin Samit (may God be pleased with him) mentioned that the Prophet (peace be upon him) forbade taking two dirhams for one dirham. A man said that when it is in cash (transaction), I do not see any harm in it. On this, Sayyidna Ubadah (may God be pleased with him) said: I say that the Messenger of God (may God bless him and grant him peace) forbade it, and you say that I do not see any harm in it. By Allah, I will never be under the same roof with you. I will not sit."
458,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Do not go near women at night.\"" The narrator said: At that time the Messenger of Allah"
459,"It was narrated from Saeed bin Musayb, may God have mercy on him, that when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came back from a journey, he descended in Maars, then ordered: \Do not go near women at night.\"" But the two men who had heard your word went out and knocked at the door of their house"
460,"Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala said that a man came to Saeed bin Al-Musayb, may God have mercy on him, to send him off for Hajj or Umrah, so Saeed bin Al-Musayb, may God have mercy on him, said: Do not leave the mosque without praying, because the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \After the call to prayer"
461,Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Do not give birth to people.
462,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: People are affected by pleasure and desire, as well as indolence and indolence."
463,"Abu Hilal al-Rasi said: I heard Imam Hasan al-Basri, may God have mercy on him, say: It is said that recite the hadeeth to people when they are drawn (with desire) towards you, and if they look around, then understand that they have some needs (i.e. not one hundred for listening to the hadeeth)."
464,"On the authority of Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Do not write from me anything other than the Holy Qur'an"
465,"It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) that the Companions (RA) asked the Prophet (PBUH) for permission to write Hadith, but he did not give them permission."
466,"Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, used to say: O Shabak! Has any hadith been returned for you? I don't want any hadith to be repeated for me too."
467,"Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi says: I heard Imam Malik bin Anas, may God have mercy on him, say that Ibn Shihab Zuhri came with a hadith, I met him on the way and held the reins, then said: O Abu Bakr! Tell me again the same hadith that you have narrated. He said: Do you want to hear it again? I asked: You did not listen again? He said no, I said: And you were not even writing? He said: No."
468,"Imam Uza'i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Qatadah used to dislike writing hadith, and when he knew that it had been written, he disliked it and would erase it with his own hand."
469,Abu al-Mughira (Hajjaj ibn Abdul Quddus) reported that Imam Uza'i (may God have mercy on him) considered it makruh (i.e. the writing of hadith).
470,It is narrated from Mansoor that Imam Ibrahim Nakhai considered the writing of knowledge to be an abomination.
471,"Imam Muhammad bin Sirin, may God have mercy on him, said: If I had to make a book, I would make a book of the letters of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace."
472,"It was narrated from Abdullah bin Aoun that I saw Hammad writing to Imam Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, so Imam Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him, said: Didn't I forbid you to write? Hammad replied that only the sides are written (i.e. the indications are written)."
473,"It was narrated from Ibrahim that Ubaidah said to me: Do not create a book on my behalf. (That is, not to write anything so that it becomes a book and remains)."
474,"Hisham bin Hasan said: I wrote down only the best hadith from Imam Muhammad bin Sirin, may God have mercy on him, then when I remembered it, I erased it."
475,Marwan bin Muhammad said: I heard: Saeed bin Abdul Aziz used to say: I have never written any hadith.
476,Ibrahim (bin Yazid) said: I never wrote any hadith.
477,"Ibrahim said: I asked Ubaidah (Ibn Umar Al-Sulmani) for a piece of leather so that I could write on it, so he said: O Ibrahim! Do not leave me any book (i.e. do not leave anything written)."
478,"(Mawquf Hadith) 'Abdullah informed us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from 'Ubaydah, similar to it."
479,"Ibrahim disliked writing hadith in copies, and used to say: It will become like a Mushaf."
480,"Yahya said: I saw in my book that Ziyad al-Katib wrote: Narrated by Abu Mushar, write it as you wish."
481,"It was narrated on the authority of Numan bin Qays that Ubaidah bin Amr called for his books before his death and erased them, and said: I am afraid that some people will find them and not put them in their proper place."
482,"Mujahid, may God have mercy on him, disliked writing things of knowledge in the copies."
483,"Imam Uza'i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This knowledge was strong as long as it was received orally from the people until it was written in the Mushaf, then the unqualified people began to take it up or enter it."
484,Yunus bin Ubayd said: Imam Hasan Basri (may Allah have mercy on him) used to write and Imam Muhammad bin Sireen (may Allah have mercy on him) neither wrote nor wrote.
485,"Ibrahim Taymi said: Sayyidna Ibn Mas'ud (RA) heard that some people had a book that they were proud of. Sayyidna Ibn Mas'ud (RA) erased it and then said: \The People of the Book perished before you because they turned to the books of their scholars and abandoned the Book of God.\"""""""
486,"Imam Muhammad bin Sirin, may God have mercy on him, said to Ubaidah (bin Amr al-Sulmani): Shall I write down what I hear from you? He said: No, I said: If you find what is written, should you read it? He said: No."
487,"Abu Nazra said: I asked Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri (RA) that you will write to us, won't you? We cannot memorize, he said: No, we will never write it down for you and we will not let what is written become the Qur'an."
488,"On the authority of Imam Uza'i, may God have mercy on him: I heard Abu Kathir say, he said: Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, used to say: Abu Hurairah does not write and does not write."
489,"It is narrated from Abu Barda that he used to write down the hadith of his father, and when Abu Musa saw him doing this, he erased it."
490,"Quraish bin Anas narrated that Ibn Aoun said to me: By Allah, I have never written any hadith, and Ibn Aoun said: Ibn Sirin, may God have mercy on him, also said: No, by Allah, I have never written any hadith."
491,"Abdullah bin Aoun said: Muhammad bin Sireen, may God have mercy on him, said to me: It was narrated from Sayyidna Zaid bin Thabit, may God be pleased with him, that Marwan bin Al-Hikam, who was the governor of Madinah, asked me to write something to him, but I did not do so. The narrator said: The Amir (respected) put a curtain between himself and the rest of the women's house (people of the house), then the governor's companions came to him at that place and started talking, then Marwan turned to his companions and said: I think we have betrayed them. Then they turned to me (Zayd bin Thabit), I said: What kind of betrayal? Said: I think we have betrayed you, said what is the matter? He said: We ordered a man to sit behind this curtain and write down whatever fatwa these people give and whatever you say."
492,Mansur (bin al-Mu'tamar) said: I told Ibrahim that Salem (Ibn Abi al-Jaad) is more perfect in hadith than you. Ibrahim said: Because Salem used to write it down.
493,"Amr bin Qays said: On the death of Sayyidna Muawiyah, I went with my father to Yazid bin Muawiyah to offer his condolences and congratulations on the caliphate. Do you see a man in his mosque saying: Watch out! One of the signs of the Day of Resurrection is that the wicked will be raised and the righteous (good people) will be overthrown. Listen! One of the signs of the Day of Judgment is that words will be expressed and actions will be preserved. Listen! Among the conditions of the Sa'at is that the \Musna'ah\"" (secondary book) will be recited and no one will change it. It was asked: What is this \""Musna'ah\""? I did not recognize who these men are. Then I narrated this hadith in Homs"
494,"Marah Hamdani said that Abu Qura Kundi brought a book from Syria and handed it over to Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he read this book and asked for a plate and water and washed it by rubbing it and said: People before you perished because of following their other books and abandoning their original book. On the authority of Hussain: Marah said: If it was something from the Book and the Sunnah, Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud would not have erased it, that inscription was from the books of the People of the Book."
495,Yahya bin Ja'da said: A shoulder bone was brought to the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he (peace be upon him) said: \It is enough for a people to go astray that they dislike what their Prophet brought and turn away from their Prophet and turn to another Prophet
496,"Ash'a'th (Ibn Abi al-Sha'a'a) narrated from his father, who was one of the disciples of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud, that I saw a scripture with a man in which it was written: \Glory be to God and praise be to God"
497,"Sayyidina Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) said: The Children of Israel wrote a book, they followed it and left the Torah."
498,"Affan (bin Abdullah bin Mardas al-Maharabi) narrated from his father (Abdullah) that I heard Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: Verily, some people listen to my speech and then go and write it down, and I do not make it lawful for anyone to write anything other than the Book of Allah."
499,"Ibn Shabarmah said: I heard Imam Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, say: I never wrote the Daraa in the white, and I never asked a person to hear any Hadith again."
500,Wahib bin Manbah narrated from his brother that he heard Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) saying: There is no one among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) who has more hadith than me except Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Amr (RA) because he used to write it down and I did not write it down.
501,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas (RA) said: I used to write down whatever I heard from the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) in order to memorize it, so the Quraysh forbade me and said: “You write down whatever you hear from the Messenger of Allah (PBUH), even though the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) is also a human being and speaks in anger and happiness. He pointed to his Blessed One and said: \Write! By the One in Whose hand is my soul"
502,"It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) that he came to the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah! I want to narrate your hadith, so if you consider it appropriate, I intend to take help from the writing of my hand along with the heart. The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \First memorize my hadith well"
503,"Abu Qubeel said: I heard Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr say: We were sitting around the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was suddenly asked: Which city will be conquered first, Constantinople or Rome? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: \No"
504,"Abdullah bin Dinar said: Umar bin Abdulaziz, may Allah have mercy on him, wrote to Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm, asking him to write down and send to us the proven hadith of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and from Umrah (Marwi), because I am afraid of the loss of knowledge."
505,Abdullah bin Dinar said that Umar bin Abdulaziz (may Allah have mercy on him) wrote to the people of Madinah to find the hadith of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and write it down.
506,"Abu Malih (Usama bin Umayr) said: People blame us for writing books, although Allah Almighty says: «﴿ Ilmuha aind Rabi fi Kitab"
507,"Sawada bin Hibban narrated that I heard Abu Ayyas Muawiya bin Qara saying: He who does not write down his knowledge, his knowledge will not remain knowledge."
508,"Abdullah bin Al-Muthani said: Thumamah bin Anas narrated to me that Sayyiduna Anas (RA) used to say to his sons: Sons! Capture this knowledge, that is, write it down."
509,Muslim Ibn Qays Al-Alawi said: I saw Aban (Ibn Abi Ayyash) writing on a (board) near Sayyiduna Anas.
510,"It is narrated from Hasan bin Jabir that he asked Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Bahli (RA) about writing down knowledge, and he replied: There is no harm in it."
511,"Bashir bin Naheek said: I used to write down what I heard from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, when I started to leave him, I took what I had written to him and read it to him and said that this is what I heard from you, he said: It is right."
512,Saeed bin Jubayr said: I used to listen to hadeeth from Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) at night and write it down on the palm of my hand.
513,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: There is nothing dear or desirable to me in life except the righteous and righteous. \Sadiqah\"" is the collection of hadiths and the scripture that I wrote from the Messenger of Allah"
514,"Abdul Malik bin Abdullah bin Abi Sufyan narrated on the authority of his uncle Amr bin Abi Sufyan that he heard Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, say: Capture knowledge through writing."
515,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said: Capture this knowledge through writing.
516,"Uthman bin Hakim narrated that I heard Saeed bin Jubayr say that I was walking along the road to Makkah with Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) and whatever hadith he narrated, I would write it down on the hand of Kajawe so that I would write it down (in a copy) in the morning."
517,"Saeed bin Jubayr said: I used to write in the Saheeh with Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) and if there was nothing else, I would also write on the shoes."
518,"Said bin Jubayr said: I used to sit near Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) and write in the Saheeh until it was full, then I would turn my shoes upside down and write under them."
519,Ubaid (bin Mehran) Muktib said: I saw people who write commentaries on Mujahid.
520,Abdullah bin Hanash said: I saw people writing on their hands with the edges of reeds near Sayyidna Bara bin Azib.
521,It was narrated from Haroon bin Antra that his father said: Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated a hadith to me. I said: Shall I write it down for you? He said: Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) allowed me to do this and did not stop me.
522,"Narrating Rajah bin Hayyah, he said: Hisham bin Abdul Malik wrote to his governor to inquire about a hadith from me. Rajah said: If it had not been written with me, I would have forgotten it."
523,"Hisham bin Ghaz said that he used to ask Ata bin Abi Rabah, may God have mercy on him, a question, and he used to write the answer he gave in front of him."
524,"Sulaiman bin Musa saw Nafi Mawly Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, he used to spell out his knowledge and he (i.e. Sulaiman) used to write in front of him."
525,"Mubarak bin Saeed narrated: Sufyan used to write hadith on the wall at night and when morning came, he would erase it and scratch what was written on the wall."
526,"Aun bin Abdullah narrated that I said to Umar bin Abdul Aziz, may God have mercy on him: So and so companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated a hadith to me. Umar bin Abdul Aziz, may God have mercy on him, recognized him. increase in this world, and decrease in the deeds of this world, and that which increases in the Hereafter is great. And indeed, vanity, abuse, and miserliness are among the things that increase in this world, but decrease in the Hereafter, and that which decreases in the Hereafter is great.”"
527,"Abu Qalaba said: Umar bin Abdul Aziz, may God have mercy on him, came out for the Zuhr prayer and he had a paper with him, then when he came for the Asr prayer, that paper was still with him, so I said: O Commander of the Faithful! What kind of book is this? He said: This is the hadith that Aoun bin Abdullah narrated to me. I liked it so I wrote it down. That is, the aforementioned hadith."
528,"Sharhabil bin Saad said that Hasan called his sons and nephews and said: Sons of me and my brother! You are the youngest of the family and soon you will be counted among the elders, so acquire knowledge, and whoever among you cannot afford tradition and memorization should write it down and keep it in his house."
529,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Jarir, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever enunciates a good word (of the Book and Sunnah) and people follow it"
530,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever calls to guidance"
531,"It was narrated on the authority of Syedna Jarir bin Abdullah (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) gave us a sermon and encouraged the people to give charity, but the people delayed until the signs of anger became visible on the face of the Prophet (PBUH). Later, a man from the Ansar came with a bag, then the people quarreled until signs of happiness were seen on the face of the Prophet (PBUH), then the Prophet (PBUH) said: There is also a reward for the one who acts, and there will be no reduction in the reward of those who act, and the one who practices evil will bear the burden of what he has done, and the one who acts upon it will also bear the burden."
532,"Hasan bin Atiya narrated: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \On the Day of Resurrection you will be rewarded the most"
533,"Sayyidina Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever calls to something"
534,"It was narrated from Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: There are four things that will be given to a person on the Day of Resurrection: a third of his wealth, if he had a obedient and obedient bearer of Allah before his death, secondly, righteous children who continue to pray for him after his death, thirdly, the good behavior that a person practices and continues to follow after his death. Four hundred men who intercede for that person will be accepted in his favor."
535,"Amish (Sulaiman bin Mehran) said: We forced Imam Ibrahim Nakhai (may God have mercy on him) to make him sit by the pillar, but he refused."
536,It was narrated from Mugheera bin Muqassim that Imam Ibrahim Nakhai (may Allah have mercy on him) used to dislike sitting next to Saria.
537,"Mugheera bin Muqsim said: Imam Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, did not recite hadiths because of anyone's request."
538,"Khaytmah said: Harith bin Qais al-Jaafi, who was one of the disciples of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, and people used to be proud of him. When one or two men would sit near him, they would start narrating a hadith to them, then when their number increased, they would stand up and leave them. (That is, he did not like to be famous among many people)."
539,"It was narrated from Ibrahim that when Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masud died, it was said to Alqamah (bin Qais): I wish you could sit (in the place of Ibn Masud) and teach the people (like him) the Sunnah. He said: Do you want my heel to be crushed? (That is, I will be tempted by those who come after me)."
540,"Salim bin Hanzala said, \We went to Sayyidna Abi bin Ka'b (RA) to talk. When he stood up"
541,It was narrated from Mansur (bin al-Mu'tamar) that Ibrahim said: They (the predecessors) disliked walking behind.
542,"Bustam bin Muslim said: When a man walked behind Imam Muhammad bin Sirin, may God have mercy on him, he would stand up and say: Do you need anything? If he had any need, he would fulfill it, yet if he followed you, he would ask: Is there any other need?"
543,"On the authority of Abu Hamza, Ibrahim said: Beware of him, lest he follow you. (That is, to avoid him from following in your footsteps)."
544,"It was narrated from Asim bin Zamra that he saw some people following Saeed bin Jubayr. The narrator said: I think Asim said: He stopped them from following him and said: This act of yours, or he said: This act of yours following me is humiliation for the follower and (follower) is a temptation for the one who is following."
545,"Abdullah bin Aoun said: I consulted Muhammad (Ibn Sirin, may God have mercy on him) about building a house in the field. He replied: When you intend to lay a foundation, let me know. So when I came to him and we both started walking, suddenly a man came and started walking behind him. Muhammad, may God have mercy on him, stood up and said: Do you need anything? He said: No, he said: Go when there is no need, then he turned towards me and said: Go, you too go, so I also left (leaving them) by another route."
546,"It was narrated from Nasir (Ibn Dhuluk) that when the people (his disciples) used to come to Rabi, may God have mercy on him, they would say: I seek refuge in Allah from your evil."
547,"Abd al-Rahman bin Bishr said: We were with Sayyidna Khabab bin Alarat, may his disciples come to him and he remained silent. It was said: Will you not narrate the hadith to your disciples? He said: I am afraid that I will tell them something that I myself do not follow."
548,"Saleh (bin Saleh bin Hay) said: I heard Imam Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, say: I wish that I would be free in my knowledge, that I would not find anything (nor be accused) and that I would not be burdened with sin."
549,It is narrated by Imam Hasan Basri (may Allah have mercy on him) that Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) was leaving when people began to follow him.
550,"Saeed bin Jubayr, may God have mercy on him, said: For the one who is being followed, there is a trial and for the one who is being followed, there is humiliation."
551,"Umm (bin Rabi'ah) said: The people were following Sayyiduna Ali (may God be pleased with him), he said: Keep away from me the tread of your shoes, for it is (something) that corrupts the hearts of foolish and humble people."
552,"It was narrated from Yazid bin Hazim that I heard Imam Hasan Basri, may God have mercy on him, say: Stealing shoes behind people prevents fools from increasing in knowledge."
553,"Leith narrated that when one or two people would come to Imam Tawas, may God have mercy on him, he would stand up and move away."
554,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Barza Aslami, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \No servant's feet will be removed on the Day of Resurrection until he is asked: In what did he spend his life? How much did he act on his knowledge? Where did he earn his wealth and in what did he spend it? And in what (work) did he use his body?\"""""""
555,"On the authority of Sayyidina Muadh bin Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: On the Day of Resurrection, when people will stand before the Lord of the Worlds, Allah will not leave His servants before asking them four things. How did you live your life? What did you use your body for? How did you earn money and what did you spend it on? And how much did you implement the knowledge you gained?"
556,"Sayyidna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) said: On the Day of Resurrection, no servant's steps will be removed until he is asked about four things, in which did he lose his life? What did you put your body in? How did you earn your wealth and where did you spend it? And how much did you act on your knowledge?"
557,"On the authority of Layth bin Abi Salim, Imam Tawas, may God have mercy on him, said to me: Learn for yourself what you have learned, because trust has been lifted from the people."
558,"On the authority of Ammara bin Mehran, Imam Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: I found a group among them, when a person worshiped, he could not be recognized by his speech, but he was recognized by his actions. This is beneficial knowledge."
559,"Abu Kash al-Sali narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Convey my message to the people"
560,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, commanded us that \people should not prevail over us in three things"
561,"Salim bin Aamir narrated that when we used to sit with Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu, he used to tell us a hadith about something very important and said: Listen and understand! And convey what you hear from us to others. Salim said: As if they were bearing witness to the knowledge they acquired."
562,"Abu Kathir narrated that my father said: I came to Sayyiduna Abu Dharr while he was sitting near the central Jamrah, and people were gathering around him asking for fatwas. Sayyiduna Abu Dharr raised his eyes and said: Are you looking after me? Even if you put a sword on my neck and I feel free to say even one word that I heard from the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, I will surely say it before my neck is cut."
563,"Abul Aaliyah said: I asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) about something, so he said: O Abul Aaliyah! Do you want to be a mufti? I said: No, but I do not believe that you should leave and we remain."
564,It was narrated from Ibrahim that Ubaidah (bin Umar al-Sulmani) used to come to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masood RA every Thursday and ask him about what he did not understand.
565,"Saeed bin Yazid said: I heard from Ikrimah, he used to say: What is the matter that you do not ask me? are you tired (You are tired)."
566,"On the authority of Yunus bin Yazid, Ibn Shahab al-Zuhri said: Knowledge is a treasure and it is opened by asking."
567,"On the authority of Jarir (bin Abdul Hameed): Imam Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, said: He who has shame and modesty has lost his knowledge."
568,"Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, said: He who has shame and modesty has lost his knowledge."
569,"On the authority of Hafs bin Umar, Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, said: Whoever is modest, his knowledge has become weak."
570,"Mujahid, may Allah have mercy on him, said: He who is ashamed and arrogant cannot acquire knowledge."
571,"Hisham bin Arwa said: His father used to gather his sons and say: Sons! Get knowledge, if you are the smallest in the congregation, then in the end you will be the greatest of others, and how ugly is the shaykh who is questioned and does not have knowledge."
572,"Ikramah (the teacher of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him) said: Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, used to put shackles on my feet and teach me the Qur'an and the Sunnah."
573,"Yahya bin Zarees narrated, I heard Sufyan saying: He who quickly became a noble was deprived of much knowledge, and he who did not become a noble remained in search of knowledge until he reached a high position."
574,"On the authority of Hussain bin Uqbah, Sayyiduna Salman (RA) said: Knowledge that is not spread is like a treasure that is not spent."
575,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \An example of knowledge that is not taken advantage of is like a treasure that is not spent in the way of Allah.\"""""""
576,"Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to his uncle Musa bin Yasar: I have heard that Sayyidna Salman (RA) wrote to Sayyidna Abu Darda’ (RA): Knowledge is like a spring into which people enter, and they all explore it, and many people benefit from it. Be that as it may, the example of a scholar is like that of a man who placed a lamp in a dark path, which gives light to every passerby, and every man prays for him."
577,"Ibrahim said: A man leaves behind three things after his death, continuous charity, the prayers of his children for him, and the knowledge that he spread, to be followed after it."
578,"On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Hurairah, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When a person dies"
579,"Narrated by Hasan: When Sayyiduna Abu Musa (RA) came to Basra, he said: Sayyidna Umar Ibn Al-Khattab (RA) has sent me to you to teach you the Book of your Lord and your Sunnah, and to make your path clear."
580,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Sukhbara, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever seeks knowledge"
581,"Abu Qalaba said: I stayed in Madinah (Taiba) for three days and got rid of all necessities, except (waiting) for a man who was expected by the people, who narrated hadith."
582,"Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir said: I heard Basr bin Ubaidullah, he used to say: I travel from city to city to hear a hadith."
583,Abul Aaliya said: We used to listen to the narrations from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) in Basra.
584,Abdullah bin Abd al-Rahman al-Qashiri said: Prophet Dawood (peace be upon him) said: \Tell the master of knowledge to make an iron staff and iron shoes
585,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) said: I searched for knowledge and found it nowhere more than among the Ansar, so I used to go to a man and ask him about it. I would be told that he was sleeping. I would make a pillow of my cloak and then lie down. How long have you been here? I used to say: I have been sitting for a long time. I would say: I wanted you to go out after fulfilling your needs."
586,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) said: I found most of the hadiths of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in this neighborhood of the Ansar. By Allah, if I went to his men, I would be told that they were asleep. If I wanted, they would have woken them up for me, but I would let them sleep until they would come out on their own and I would recite the hadiths from them well in this way."
587,"Abu Salamah (bin Abdul Rahman bin Awf) said: If I had taken the companionship of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may God be pleased with him), I would have acquired a lot of knowledge from him."
588,"Imam al-Zuhri (may Allah have mercy on him) said: If I used to go to the door of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, he would sit there out of respect for his majesty, although he would enter (inside) if he wanted to."
589,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) said: When the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) died, I said to a man of the Ansar: O brother! Let us inquire about the Companions of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, today they are present in large numbers. He replied: Son of Abbas! What strange thing do you say? Do you think that people will need you in the presence of so many Companions of the Messenger? So they gave up and I focused on questioning, so when a hadith reached me, I used to go to him (Ansari brother), he used to say Qilaula, put a pillow on his door, and the wind would cover my face with dust. Why did you come? Had someone been sent, I would have attended myself, I would have said: No, I am more in need to come to you, then I would have asked them about this hadith. Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: He (the Companions of Ansari) lived for a long time until, seeing me, people flocked to me. He said: This young man was wiser than me."
590,"Abdullah bin Burida said: One of the companions of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to Sayyidna Fazalah bin Ubaid, who was in Egypt. When he reached him, Sayyidna Fazalah, may God be pleased with him, was watering his camel. Said: What is that? Said: This and this hadith."
591,"On the authority of Abdul Ali, Imam Hasan Basri (may Allah have mercy on him) entered the market, asked a man to buy a piece of cloth, and he said: It is worth this much for you. After that, they were not seen buying and selling in the market until they met Allah."
592,"Abu Mushar (Ziyad bin Kalib) said: Imam Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, did not buy from anyone he knew."
593,"It was narrated from Ubayd bin Al-Hasan that Musab bin Zubair distributed some wealth to the reciters of Kufa at the beginning of Ramadan, and sent two thousand dirhams to Abd al-Rahman bin Muqal and said to take help from this wealth in this holy month, but Abd al-Rahman bin Muqal returned those dirhams and said: We do not recite the Qur’an for him."
594,Ubaidullah bin Umar narrated that Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) asked Sayyidna Abdullah bin Salam (RA): Who are the people of knowledge? Said: Those who act according to knowledge. Asked: What removes knowledge from people's hearts? He said: Greed.
595,"It is narrated from Zayd that nothing is better than anything, from humility to knowledge."
596,Narrated by Asim Al-Ahool: Amir Shaabi said: The adornment of knowledge is the patience of the people of knowledge.
597,"On the authority of Salama bin Wahram, Imam Taaws, may God have mercy on him, said: Knowledge is not gained in anything like a sack."
598,Narrated by Ibn Shabarmah: Sha'bi said: The adornment of knowledge is the arrogance of the people of knowledge.
599,"On the authority of Ya'ali bin Muqassim: Wahib bin Munba said: Wisdom resides in a gentle, tolerant and satisfied heart."
600,Sufyan used to say: Ubaidullah (Ibn Umar) said: You have tarnished knowledge and wasted its light.
601,"On the authority of Umm al-Maradi, Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Learn knowledge, and when you have acquired knowledge, protect it."
602,"On the authority of Fazil bin Ghazwan: Ali bin Hussain, may God have mercy on him, said: He who laughs once has lost knowledge once. That is, laughing and laughing is not the glory of the world."
603,"On the authority of Sufyan, Sayyiduna Umar (RA) said to Sayyidna Ka'b (RA): Who are the people of knowledge? He said: Those who act according to knowledge. He said: And what removed knowledge from the hearts of scholars? Answered: (Greed) Greed."
604,"Abu Ayyas said: I was staying with Amr bin Nu'man when the messenger of Musab bin Zubair came to him in Ramadan with two thousand dirhams and said: The Amir (respected) has greeted you and has ordered that we do not leave any honorable reciter without any gifts, so let him accept the expenses of this month. Amr bin Nu'man said: Give my greetings to this noble emir, and say to him, By Allah, we have not read the Qur'an (the Noble Qur'an) for the sake of the world and dirhams."
605,"Narrated by Sayyidna Muqadam bin Maadikarb, may Allah be pleased with him: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, prohibited certain things on the day of Khaibar, such as donkeys, then he said: \Soon a man will recline on his musnad while narrating my hadith and say: We have the Book of Allah between you and us"
606,"On the authority of Imam Uza'i, may God have mercy on him, Yahya bin Abi Kathir said: The Sunnah is the interpreter and judge of the Qur'an, and the Qur'an is not the judge of the rate of the Sunnah."
607,"On the authority of Imam Uza'i, may God have mercy on him, Hasan said: Gabriel (peace be upon him) used to bring the Sunnah to the Messenger of God, just as he used to bring the Qur'an to him."
608,"It was narrated from Imam Uza'i, may God have mercy on him: Makhool, may God have mercy on him, said: There are two types of Sunnah, one is that which is obligatory to hold (hold) and to leave it is disbelief, and the other is that Sunnah that is virtuous to be followed and there is no problem in abandoning it."
609,"Saeed bin Jubayr, may Allah have mercy on him, narrated a hadith of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace. He said: I am narrating to you the hadith of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace."
610,"On the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When the hadith of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, is narrated to you, be sure that it is very agreeable, very instructive, and very pious."
611,"On the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Salami, Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When the hadith of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, is narrated to you, be sure that it is the most guided, the most pious, and the most agreeable."
612,"When Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) used to narrate the hadith of the Prophet, he would say: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \He who tells me a lie on purpose"
613,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, used to say: When you hear me narrating the hadith of the Prophet and you do not find it in the Book of Allah, and people do not find it better, then know that I have lied about you."
614,"On the authority of Sulaiman Al-Ahul, Ikrima (Mouli Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him) said: The most fearless about a scholar is his family."
615,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Discuss the hadith, because the hadith reminds one of the hadith."
616,The above-mentioned hadith of Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) from the second chain of transmission.
617,"Abu Nazrah narrates that Sayyidna Abu Saeed al-Khudri said: Talk in hadith, because one hadith reminds another hadith."
618,Abu Nazrah narrates from Sayyidna Abu Saeed (may God be pleased with him) and it has more words than this.
619,"(Mawquf hadith) — Ibn ʿUlayyah narrated from al-Jurayrī, from Abū Naḍrah, from Abū Saʿīd…"
620,"On the authority of Abu Salamat Abu Nazrah, Sayyiduna Abu Saeed (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the same saying."
621,"It was narrated on the authority of Amr bin Muslim that Imam Taaws, may God have mercy on him, said to me: Take us and let us sit with the people (i.e. for discussion of hadith)."
622,"On the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, may God have mercy on him, Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: Repeat the hadith so that you do not forget, because the hadith is not as complete and safe as the Qur'an. If you do not discuss it, you will forget it. Also, none of you should say that I narrated a hadith yesterday, so I will not narrate it today, rather, if all the previous hadiths were narrated, then narrate them today and also narrate the next ones tomorrow."
623,"It was narrated from Saeed bin Jubayr, may God have mercy on him, that Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: Repeat the hadith and memorize it, if you do not remember it, you will forget it, and no man should say after narrating a hadith that I have narrated it once, because the one who heard the hadith first will increase in his knowledge, and the one who did not hear it will hear it now."
624,"On the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laili said: Discuss, the way to keep the hadith alive is to repeat it and discuss."
625,"It is narrated from Ibrahim that al-Qamah said: Discuss the hadith, its remembrance is its life."
626,"On the authority of Sufyan bin Uyaina, Ziyad bin Saad said: Ibn Shihab al-Zuhri used to recite hadith to the villagers as well."
627,Amish (Sulaiman bin Mehran) said: Ismail bin Raja used to gather the children of the Munshis and recite the hadith to them.
628,"It was narrated from Abu Abdullah al-Shaqri that Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him, said: Narrate your hadith to everyone, whether he wants to hear it or not, because it will become the original for you even if you are reading it while looking at the original."
629,"On the authority of Ata (Ibn Abi Rabah): Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When you hear a hadith from us, discuss it among yourselves."
630,"Hashim said: Yunus bin Ubaid reported that we used to go to Hasan, may God have mercy on him, and when we returned from him, we used to talk to each other."
631,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When one of you wants to narrate a hadith, he should repeat this hadith three times."
632,"Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laili said: The way to keep the hadith alive is to discuss it. Abdullah bin Shaddad said to him: May Allah have mercy on you, how many hadiths are there that were erased, you revived them in my heart."
633,"Narrated Muhammad bin Fuzil, his father said: Harith bin Yazid Aqli, Ibn Shabarmah and Qaqaa bin Yazid and Mughira would sit in Fiqh (discussion) after the Isha prayer, and then the morning call to prayer would separate them."
634,"Malik bin Ismail reported that I heard the participant saying, he said through Laith, two of Ata, Taaws and Mujahid said: There is no harm in staying up at night in matters of jurisprudence."
635,"On the authority of Leith, Mujahid said: There is no harm in staying awake during legal discussions."
636,"On the authority of Ibn Juraj, Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Reading together for an hour is better than worshiping the whole night."
637,"Ata said: We used to go to Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may God be pleased with him), and when we returned from him, we would discuss with each other, and Abu al-Zubayr was the most memorizer of hadith among us."
638,"Marwan bin Muhammad reported that I heard from Layth bin Sa'd, he said: Ibn Shahab (Zuhri) was performing ablution one night after Isha when he started memorizing the hadith, then he kept memorizing it while sitting until morning. Marwan said: He kept discussing hadith."
639,"On the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, Zahri said: When I used to meet Ubaidullah bin Utbah, it would seem as if I had split the sea."
640,Uthman bin Abdullah said: Harith Aqli and his companions used to sit at night and memorize jurisprudential issues.
641,"On the authority of Abul Ahus, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) said: Remember the hadith, because its life is to remember it or discuss it."
642,"It is narrated from Aoun bin Abdullah that the disciples of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) came to him and he said to them: Do you hold a meeting? He replied: We do not leave him. He said: Do you visit each other? Answered: Yes, O Abu Abdul Rahman! If one of us does not see his partner, he goes to the end of the cup to see him. Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud Radiyallahu Anhu said: As long as you continue to do this, you will live well."
643,"On the authority of Imam Uza'i, may God have mercy on him, Imam Zuhri, may God have mercy on him, said: The bane of knowledge is forgetfulness and abandonment of conversation."
644,"On the authority of Qasim bin Abd al-Rahman Mas’udi, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (RA) said: The calamity of hadith is nasyan (i.e. forgetting)."
645,"On the authority of Hakeem bin Jabir, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: Everything has a calamity, the calamity of knowledge is forgetfulness."
646,"On the authority of Amish, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The bane of knowledge is forgetfulness"
647,"On the authority of Abu Hamza Al-Tamar, Hassan Basri, may God have mercy on him, said: The evil of knowledge is forgetfulness."
648,"On the authority of Ibn Burida, Sayyiduna Ali (RA) said: Remember (repeat) this (knowledge) hadith, visit each other, if you do not do this, it (knowledge) will be lost."
649,"On the authority of Sufyan, may God have mercy on him, Imam al-Zuhri, may God have mercy on him, said: I thought that I had completed knowledge, but when I entered the congregation of Ubaidullah (bin Abdullah bin Masud), I felt that I was only in one of the many valleys or valleys of knowledge (i.e., my knowledge was very little compared to him)."
